gistered.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Element.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"show\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.show\",\"slug\":\"show\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when showing the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when showing the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n This table shows possible `effectName` values\\r\\n and their corresponding names in the editor:\\r\\n\\r\\n | Effect Name Value    | Editor Animation Name |\\r\\n | -------------------- | -------------------------- |\\r\\n | `\\\"arc\\\"`              | Arc-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"bounce\\\"`           | Bounce-In                  |\\r\\n | `\\\"fade\\\"`             | Fade-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"flip\\\"`             | Flip-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"float\\\"`            | Float-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"fly\\\"`              | Fly-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"fold\\\"`             | Fold-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"glide\\\"`            | Glide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"puff\\\"`             | Puff-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"roll\\\"`             | Reveal                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"slide\\\"`            | Slide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"spin\\\"`             | Spin-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"turn\\\"`             | Turn-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"zoom\\\"`             | Expand-In                  |\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, the `show ()` function will not make an element visible for a given breakpoint\\r\\n\u003e   if the element has been set to \\\"**Hide** for that breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\\r\\n\u003e   Calling `show()` however, will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `show()` and `hide()` with **Hide** and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"accessibility\",\"slug\":\"accessibility\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Accessibility\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Button.Accessibility\"},\"description\":\"Sets and gets the [Accessible Rich Internet Application (ARIA) attributes](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Attributes) of the element.\\r\\n\\r\\nARIA attributes are a set of properties that define ways to make web content and applications more accessible to people with disabilities. The properties provide additional information about the structure, behavior, and state of elements to assistive technologies such as screen readers, braille displays, and voice control software. Set the accessibility properties to design your elements to be more inclusive and usable to users with visual, auditory, motor, and or cognitive disabilities. The accessibility object only affects how assistive technologies read and present site content to users. It doesn't affect the appearance, functionality, or SEO of your site. \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** Incorrect use of ARIA can worsen accessibility for assistive technology users. Use carefully and test with assistive technologies. \\r\\n\\r\\nLearn more about [ARIA attributes](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA).\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"effects\",\"slug\":\"effects\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's effects\",\"content\":\"let myEffects = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").effects;\\n\\nlet firstEffect = myEffects[0];\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Effects\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Effects.Effects\"},\"description\":\"An object containing functionality for displaying the [effects](https://support.wix.com/en/article/studio-editor-adding-a-preset-click-or-hover-interaction) defined for an element using Wix Studio.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** This API can only be used in Wix Studio.\"},{\"name\":\"enabled\",\"slug\":\"enabled\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's enabled status\",\"content\":\"let isEnabled = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled; // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is enabled or disabled.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `enabled` is `true`, users can interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `enabled` is `false`, users cannot interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n When an element is disabled:\\r\\n\\r\\n + Its color is faded or grayed out.\\r\\n + Animations that the element normally exhibits when being interacting\\r\\n   with do not occur.\\r\\n + Actions that the element has been configured to perform, such as\\r\\n   opening a link, do not occur.\\r\\n + Event handlers that have been bound to the element, such as with\\r\\n   `onMouseIn`, do not run.\\r\\n + If the element is an input element, such as a dropdown or text box,\\r\\n   users cannot interact with it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `enabled` property of an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`enable()`](#enable) or [`disable()`](#disable) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `enabled` property can also be set in the Editor using the Properties and Events panel.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"icon\",\"slug\":\"icon\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the icon image displayed on the button.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `icon` property defines the vector image used as the button’s icon.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting `icon` changes the button icon to the image indicated by the new value.\\r\\nGetting the `icon` property returns the location of the icon image file.\\r\\nTo delete a button's icon set `icon` to `null`, `undefined`, or an empty string.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following formats are supported:\\r\\n + Vector images from the Media Manager: `wix:vector://v1//`\\r\\n + Vector images from the web: `http(s)://`\\r\\n + Vector XML string: `...`\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** [Image Buttons](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-adding-and-setting-up-an-image-button) don't support this property.\"},{\"name\":\"iconCollapsed\",\"slug\":\"icon-collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the button’s icon is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `iconCollapsed` is `true`, the icon isn't displayed in the button under any circumstances. \\r\\n\\r\\nIf `iconCollapsed` is `false`, the icon is displayed unless the icon's button is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo set the iconCollapsed property on an element, use the element's [collapseIcon()](#collapseIcon) and [expandIcon()](#expandIcon) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** \\r\\n\u003e * A collapsed icon doesn't take up any space in the button.\\r\\n\u003e * If you delete a button's icon, `iconCollapsed` retains the deleted icon's final state.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"},{\"name\":\"label\",\"slug\":\"label\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets a button's label.\"},{\"name\":\"link\",\"slug\":\"link\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the button's link.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen the button is clicked, the browser navigates to the `link` location.\\r\\n\\r\\n The different types of links you can use are:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `/localPageURL`: another page on your site\\r\\n + `/`: your site's home page\\r\\n + `http(s)://`: an external web address\\r\\n + `wix:document://`: a document stored in the Media Manager\\r\\n + `mailto:?subject=`: an email\\r\\n + `tel:`: a phone number\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n The `link` property attempts to properly encode the URL value that\\r\\n you set. For example, `.../some page` is encoded to `.../some%20page`.\\r\\n However, some URLs do not have one unambiguous encoding. In those cases\\r\\n it is up to you to encode the URL to reflect your intentions. Because of\\r\\n these situations, it is a best practice to always encode URLs before you\\r\\n set them as the value of the `link` property. Regardless of how you set\\r\\n the `link` property, when you get its value, it returns an encoded URL.\\r\\n\\r\\n Note that Wix URLs do not contain spaces. A page which has spaces in its\\r\\n name has its spaces replaced with dashes (`-`). Similarly,\\r\\n a [dynamic page URL](https://support.wix.com/en/article/creating-a-unique-dynamic-page-url) which \\r\\n contains the value of a field in your collection with spaces\\r\\n has its spaces replaced with dashes (`-`).\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** Make sure to set your button link before running (and not inside) the [`onClick()`](/$w/button/on-click) event handler.\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rel\",\"slug\":\"rel\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the link rel from an element\",\"content\":\"let rel = $w('#myElement').rel; // \\\"noopener\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the link rel for an element\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').rel = 'sponsored';\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets or sets the relationship between the link's source page and the target page.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `rel` property provides additional context to search engines and browsers about how they \\r\\nshould treat the link, influencing SEO, security, and other link behavior. \\r\\n\\r\\n Supported values:\\r\\n \\r\\n + `'noopener'`: Prevents the target page from accessing the source page with the\\r\\n[`window.opener`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/opener) property, \\r\\nreducing the risk of malicious code. \\r\\n + `'noreferrer'`: Prevents the browser from sending referrer information, such as the URL of \\r\\nthe source page, to the target page. This enhances user privacy by ensuring the target page can't \\r\\ntrack the origin of the visit.\\r\\n + `'nofollow'`: Tells search engines not to pass SEO link equity to the target page. This helps \\r\\nprevent the manipulation of search rankings and maintains the integrity of your site's SEO.\\r\\n + `'sponsored'`: Indicates that the link is part of a paid or promotional arrangement, \\r\\nensuring transparency and compliance with search engine guidelines.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element can have multiple `rel` values as a single string with each value separated by a space. \\r\\nFor example, `'nofollow sponsored'`. \\r\\n\\r\\n The default value for external web links (starting with `http://` and `https://`) is `'noopener'`.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"style\",\"slug\":\"style\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Style\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Style.Style\"},\"description\":\"Gets an object containing information about the button's styles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following styles can be used with buttons:\\r\\n\\r\\n + [`backgroundColor`]($w.Style.html#backgroundColor)\\r\\n + [`borderColor`]($w.Style.html#borderColor)\\r\\n + [`borderRadius`]($w.Style.html#borderRadius)\\r\\n + [`borderWidth`]($w.Style.html#borderWidth)\\r\\n + [`color`]($w.Style.html#color)\\r\\n + [`hover`]($w.Style.html#hover)\\r\\n + [`disabled`]($w.Style.html#disabled)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting or setting a button's `hover` and `disabled` styles affects the button's \\r\\n appearance only in those respective states. All other available styles apply solely \\r\\n to the button's regular state. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** Not all styles can be used on all button designs. To determine which styles\\r\\n work with a specific button design, go to the **Button Design** panel in\\r\\n the Editor, choose a design, and click **Customize Design**. The design\\r\\n options that you see in the **Button Design** panel for your particular\\r\\n button are the styles you can use in your code.\"},{\"name\":\"tabIndex\",\"slug\":\"tab-index\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the tab index of an element on a site page.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `tabIndex` property determines the order in which elements can be focused on or selected using the tab key on the keyboard. By default, web browsers only assign a tab index to interactive elements such as links and form controls. When set to `0`, the element becomes part of the keyboard tab and focus order. When set to `-1`, the element isn't part of the keyboard focus order but can still become focusable using the [`focus()`](#focus) function.\\r\\n\\r\\nSupported values: `-1`, `0`\"},{\"name\":\"target\",\"slug\":\"target\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the link target from an element\",\"content\":\"let url = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").target; // \\\"_blank\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the link target for an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").target = \\\"_blank\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set an element to open an external web link in a new browser page when clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").link = \\\"http://wix.com\\\";\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").target = \\\"_blank\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the target of the element's link.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element's `target` determines where its [link](#link) opens. The\\r\\n target can be set so the [link](#link) opens in the current page or\\r\\n in a new page.\\r\\n\\r\\n Supported values are:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"_blank\\\"`: The link opens in a new tab or window.\\r\\n + `\\\"_self\\\"`: The link opens in the tab or window.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:**  Link targets are only supported for external web links\\r\\n (e.g. `http://www.wix.com`).\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"}]},\"Button.Accessibility\":{\"name\":\"Accessibility\",\"fqn\":\"Button.Accessibility\",\"slug\":\"accessibility\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"ariaDescribedBy\",\"slug\":\"aria-described-by\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CollapsibleText\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CollapsibleText.CollapsibleText\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Text\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Text.Text\"}]},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the contextual description of an element by referencing another element by ID. `ariaDescribedBy` can reference either a single text element or a collapsible text element. Both visible and non-visible text elements can be referenced. The contextual description can include descriptive text, instructions, or error messages that give more context to the element's label.  \\r\\n\\r\\nExample: `$w(“#myElement”).accessibility.ariaDescribedBy = $w(\\\"#text1\\\");`\"},{\"name\":\"ariaExpanded\",\"slug\":\"aria-expanded\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates to assistive technology users whether the element is currently expanded or collapsed. `ariaExpanded` helps screen readers understand when content is displayed or hidden as a result of user interaction on your site. If `ariaExpanded` isn't explicitly set, the default is `undefined` and the property isn't read by assistive technologies.\"},{\"name\":\"ariaHasPopup\",\"slug\":\"aria-has-popup\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Indicates to assistive technology users whether an element triggers an interactive popup such as a menu or dropdown. If `ariaHasPopup` isn't explicitly set, the default is `undefined` and the property isn't read by assistive technologies.\\r\\n\\r\\nSupported values: `'true'`, `'false'`\"},{\"name\":\"ariaLabel\",\"slug\":\"aria-label\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the [accessible name](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/practices/names-and-descriptions/), a concise and descriptive label, of the element. Use `ariaLabel` when an element, such as an icon button, doesn't have a visual text label present, or has a label that should be overridden to provide clearer context. \\r\\n\\r\\nMax: 1000 characters\"},{\"name\":\"ariaLabelledBy\",\"slug\":\"aria-labelled-by\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CollapsibleText\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CollapsibleText.CollapsibleText\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Text\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Text.Text\"}]},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the accessible name or contextual label of an element by referencing another element by ID. `ariaLabelledBy` can reference either a single text element or a collapsible text element. Both visible and non-visible text elements can be referenced. When an element's accessible name is set using `ariaLabelledBy`, it takes precedence over any label set using the `ariaLabel` property. Make sure that any element referenced by `ariaLabelledBy` is present in the DOM to avoid errors and confusion for assistive technology users. \\r\\n\\r\\nExample: `$w(“#myElement”).accessibility.ariaLabelledBy = $w(\\\"#text1\\\");`\"},{\"name\":\"ariaPressed\",\"slug\":\"aria-pressed\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Indicates to assistive technology users whether the element is currently pressed. `ariaPressed` is only relevant for buttons that act as toggles or have a pressed/unpressed state. If `ariaPressed` isn't explicitly set, the default is `undefined` and the property isn't read by assistive technologies. \\r\\n\\r\\nSupported values: `'true'`, `'false'`\"}]},\"Captcha.ErrorHandler\":{\"name\":\"ErrorHandler\",\"fqn\":\"Captcha.ErrorHandler\",\"slug\":\"error-handler\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[],\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}},\"Captcha.TimeoutHandler\":{\"name\":\"TimeoutHandler\",\"fqn\":\"Captcha.TimeoutHandler\",\"slug\":\"timeout-handler\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[],\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}},\"Captcha.VerifiedHandler\":{\"name\":\"VerifiedHandler\",\"fqn\":\"Captcha.VerifiedHandler\",\"slug\":\"verified-handler\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[],\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}},{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}]}},\"CartIcon.AddToCartItem\":{\"name\":\"AddToCartItem\",\"fqn\":\"CartIcon.AddToCartItem\",\"slug\":\"add-to-cart-item\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"options\",\"slug\":\"options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"AddToCartOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CartIcon.AddToCartOptions\"},\"description\":\"Specific product options to add to the cart.\"},{\"name\":\"productId\",\"slug\":\"product-id\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The ID of the product to add to the cart.\"},{\"name\":\"quantity\",\"slug\":\"quantity\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"The number of product units to add to the cart.\"}]},\"CartIcon.AddToCartOptions\":{\"name\":\"AddToCartOptions\",\"fqn\":\"CartIcon.AddToCartOptions\",\"slug\":\"add-to-cart-options\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"choices\",\"slug\":\"choices\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"object\"},\"description\":\"Product options to use when adding the product to the cart.\\r\\nThe object contains key:value pairs where the key is the option name and the value is the chosen option value.\"},{\"name\":\"customTextFields\",\"slug\":\"custom-text-fields\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"AddToCartCustomTextField\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CartIcon.AddToCartCustomTextField\"}},\"description\":\"Custom text fields to use when adding the product to the cart.\"}]},\"CartIcon.AddToCartCustomTextField\":{\"name\":\"AddToCartCustomTextField\",\"fqn\":\"CartIcon.AddToCartCustomTextField\",\"slug\":\"add-to-cart-custom-text-field\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"title\",\"slug\":\"title\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Custom text field title.\"},{\"name\":\"value\",\"slug\":\"value\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Custom text field value.\"}]},\"Chatbox.ChannelInfo\":{\"name\":\"ChannelInfo\",\"fqn\":\"Chatbox.ChannelInfo\",\"slug\":\"channel-info\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"channelId\",\"slug\":\"channel-id\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"ID of a chat channel.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Type of chat channel.\\r\\n One of the following:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"Focused\\\"`: Currently focused channel.\\r\\n + `\\\"Business\\\"`: Business channel.\"}]},\"Chatbox.Channel\":{\"name\":\"Channel\",\"fqn\":\"Chatbox.Channel\",\"slug\":\"channel\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"displayData\",\"slug\":\"display-data\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"DisplayData\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Chatbox.DisplayData\"},\"description\":\"Display information associated with the channel.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"ID of the channel.\"},{\"name\":\"messages\",\"slug\":\"messages\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Message\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Chatbox.Message\"}},\"description\":\"An array of messages sent over the channel. Currently only the last message is included.\"}]},\"Chatbox.DisplayData\":{\"name\":\"DisplayData\",\"fqn\":\"Chatbox.DisplayData\",\"slug\":\"display-data\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"image\",\"slug\":\"image\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The image associated with the channel.\\r\\n One of the following:\\r\\n\\r\\n + For private social channels, the image associated with the site member's account. If there is no image associated with the account, defaults to the avatar image.\\r\\n + For group social channels, the image associated with the chat group.\\r\\n + For business channels, `image` is not currently supported.\"},{\"name\":\"initials\",\"slug\":\"initials\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Only supported for business channels. Initials of the site's business.\"},{\"name\":\"name\",\"slug\":\"name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"For social channels, the member's name or chat group name. For business channels, the site's [display name](wix-site-backend.generalInfo.html#getSiteDisplayName).\"}]},\"Chatbox.Message\":{\"name\":\"Message\",\"fqn\":\"Chatbox.Message\",\"slug\":\"message\",\"actions\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"channelId\",\"slug\":\"channel-id\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"ID of the channel on which the message was sent.\"},{\"name\":\"createdAt\",\"slug\":\"created-at\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"DATE\"},\"description\":\"Date and time the message was sent.\"},{\"name\":\"metadata\",\"slug\":\"metadata\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"object\"},\"description\":\"An object representing additional contextual message information included in a chat message. Only relevant for messages sent using the backend [`sendMessage()`](wix-chat-backend.html#sendMessage) function. Site visitors do not see metadata.\"},{\"name\":\"participantId\",\"slug\":\"participant-id\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The sender's member ID. For a message sent from the sit