ch element is currently in focus or active.\\r\\n\\r\\nSupported values: \\r\\n- `'true'`: Represents the current element in an unordered set of related elements.\\r\\n- `'false'`: Indicates that the element in a set is not currently active or selected.\\r\\n- `'page'`: Represents the current page in a multi-page site.\\r\\n- `'step'`: Marks the currently active step in a multi-step process such as a checkout flow.\\r\\n- `'date'`: Represents the currently selected date in a calendar.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `ariaCurrent` isn't explicitly set, the default is `undefined` and the property isn't read by assistive technologies.\"},{\"name\":\"ariaDescribedBy\",\"slug\":\"aria-described-by\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CollapsibleText\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CollapsibleText.CollapsibleText\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Text\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Text.Text\"}]},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the contextual description of an element by referencing another element by ID. `ariaDescribedBy` can reference either a single text element or a collapsible text element. Both visible and non-visible text elements can be referenced. The contextual description can include descriptive text, instructions, or error messages that give more context to the element's label.  \\r\\n\\r\\nExample: `$w(“#myElement”).accessibility.ariaDescribedBy = $w(\\\"#text1\\\");`\"},{\"name\":\"ariaHidden\",\"slug\":\"aria-hidden\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates whether the element is visible to or hidden from users that rely on assistive technologies. Use `ariaHidden` to hide decorative, redundant, or off-screen content from screen readers. When `true`, the element is hidden from assistive technologies but remains visible in the DOM. When `false`, the element is exposed to assistive techno