01f8efe0cad2.jpg/flowers.jpg#originWidth=1970\u0026originHeight=1120\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set the background image to be an image from the web\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").background.src = \\\"http://placehold.it/250x250\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BackgroundOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Background.BackgroundOptions\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets an object containing information about the element's background.\"},{\"name\":\"children\",\"slug\":\"children\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's children\",\"content\":\"let myChildren = $w(\\\"#myContainer\\\").children;\\n\\nlet firstChild = myChildren[0];\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\"}},\"description\":\"Gets an array of the elements that are contained within the element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements, such as pages, headers, footers, and boxes, can contain\\r\\n other elements. This occurs when you drag an element onto a container\\r\\n element and [attach it](https://www.wix.com/support/html5/article/attaching-elements-to-a-box).\\r\\n These attached elements are considered the parent element's children.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou c