n\\r\\n If blur() is called on an element that is not in focus, it has no effect.\\r\\n The element in focus remains in focus and the `onBlur` event handlers\\r\\n are not called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"focus\",\"fqn\":\"FocusMixin.focus\",\"slug\":\"focus\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Place focus on an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").focus();\"}],\"description\":\"Places focus on the element.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `focus()` function places focus on the element and fires a `focus`\\r\\n event.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `focus` event handlers set on this element by the [onFocus( )](#onFocus)\\r\\n function or in the Editor are called.\\r\\n\\r\\n Receiving focus through a call to this function is equivalent to\\r\\n a user clicking on or tabbing to the element manually.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onBlur\",\"fqn\":\"FocusMixin.onBlur\",\"slug\":\"on-blur\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has lost focus\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onBlur( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element loses focus.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element loses focus.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element loses focus (blurs) through user actions,\\r\\n such as clicking and tabbing, or programmatically, using the\\r\\n [`blur()`](#blur) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** `onBlur()` has no effect when applied to [RadioButtonGroup]($w.RadioButtonGroup.html) elements.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onFocus\",\"fqn\":\"FocusMixin.onFocus\",\"slug\":\"on-focus\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has received focus\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onFocus( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element receives focus.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element receives focus.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives focus through user actions,\\r\\n such as clicking and tabbing, or programmatically, using the\\r\\n [focus( )](#focus) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** `onFocus()` has no effect when applied to [RadioButtonGroup]($w.RadioButtonGroup.html) elements.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onClick\",\"slug\":\"on-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Change the background color of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').onClick((event) =\u003e {\\n  const clickedElement = event.target;\\n  clickedElement.style.backgroundColor = 'blue';\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `click` event when a user clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** To avoid unpredictable behavior, don't set redirect links in the editor for elements that already have an `onClick` event handler.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onDblClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onDblClick\",\"slug\":\"on-dbl-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was double-clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onDblClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is double-clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `dblClick` event when a user double-clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nAn appointment field contains a date picker, time picker, and a timezone dropdown.\\nUse an appointment field to schedule appointments by setting the [`dateTimeRanges`]($w/appointment-field/date-time-ranges)property for times when appointments are available, or just use it as a date and time picker.  Set days of the week that are not selectable for appointments by using [`disabledDaysOfWeek`]($w/appointment-field/disabled-days-of-week) and set the earliest and latest dates that you can select using [`minDate`]($w/appointment-field/min-date) and [`maxDate`]($w/appointment-field/max-date).\\n\\nUse the time zone dropdown to display the dates and times in the selected time zone. The default time zone that is used when setting the [`dateTimeRanges`]($w/appointment-field/date-time-ranges) property is the site's time zone, set in the [Language \u0026 Region](https://www.wix.com/my-account/site-selector/?buttonText=Select%20Site\u0026title=Select%20a%20Site\u0026autoSelectOnSingleSite=true\u0026actionUrl=https:%2F%2Fwww.wix.com%2Fdashboard%2F%7B%7BmetaSiteId%7D%7D%2Fsettings/language-and-region/) settings page.\\nThe time zone for the [`value`]($w/appointment-field/value) property is according to the browser's locale and timezone.\\n\\n![Appointment Field](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_appointmentfield.png \\\"Appointment Field\\\")\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"dateTimeRanges\",\"slug\":\"date-time-ranges\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's time ranges\",\"content\":\"let myDateTimeRanges = $w('#myAppointmentField').dateTimeRanges\\n\\n/* myDateTimeRanges:\\n *\\n * {\\n *   \\\"type\\\": \\\"enabledRanges\\\",\\n *   \\\"payload\\\": [\\n *     {\\n *       \\\"startDateTime\\\": \\\"Tue Mar 29 2022 10:00:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\",\\n *       \\\"endDateTime\\\": \\\"Tue Mar 29 2022 11:00:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\"\\n *     },\\n *     {\\n *       \\\"startDateTime\\\": \\\"Wed Mar 30 2022 10:00:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\",\\n *       \\\"endDateTime\\\": \\\"Wed Mar 30 2022 11:00:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\"\\n *     },\\n *     {\\n *       \\\"startDateTime\\\": \\\"Thu Mar 31 2022 03:30:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\",\\n *       \\\"endDateTime\\\": \\\"Thu Mar 31 2022 05:27:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\"\\n *     },\\n *     {\\n *       \\\"startDateTime\\\": \\\"Thu Mar 31 2022 10:15:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\",\\n *       \\\"endDateTime\\\": \\\"Thu Mar 31 2022 12:00:00 GMT+0900 (Japan Standard Time)\\\"\\n *     }\\n *   ]\\n * }\\n */\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's time ranges\",\"content\":\"const myEnabledDates = [\\n  {\\n    \\\"startDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-28T20:00-0500\\\"),\\n    \\\"endDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-28T21:00-0500\\\")\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"startDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-29T20:00-0500\\\"),\\n    \\\"endDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-29T21:00-0500\\\")\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"startDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-30T13:30-0500\\\"),\\n    \\\"endDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-30T15:27-0500\\\")\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"startDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-30T20:15-0500\\\"),\\n    \\\"endDateTime\\\": new Date(\\\"2022-03-30T22:00-0500\\\")\\n  }\\n];\\n\\n$w('#myAppointmentField').dateTimeRanges = {\\n  type: 'enabledRanges',\\n  payload: myEnabledDates\\n};\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"dateTimeRangeInfo\",\"referenceFqn\":\"AppointmentField.dateTimeRangeInfo\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets a list of dates and times that a site visitor can select.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `dateTimeRanges` property sets a list of dates and times that can be selected from the appointment field's date and time picker elements. Times can be specified for any timezone and are displayed according to the value in the timezone dropdown.\\r\\n\\r\\nGetting the `dateTimeRanges` property returns the list of dates and times that were set for the appointment field. The returned dates and times are according to the browser's locale and timezone.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** Setting `dateTimeRanges` overrides the settings panel in the editor for enabled times and enabled date ranges. Dates that have been disabled in the editor are not overridden.\"},{\"name\":\"disabledDaysOfWeek\",\"slug\":\"disabled-days-of-week\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's disabledDaysOfWeek property\",\"content\":\"let disabledDays = $w('#myAppointmentField').disabledDaysOfWeek; // [0, 2]\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's disabledDaysOfWeek property\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').disabledDaysOfWeek = [0, 2];\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"}},\"description\":\"Sets or gets a list of days in the week that are not selectable.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `disabledDaysOfWeek` property sets a list of days of the week that can't be selected in the appointment field's date element.\\r\\nWeekdays are numbered 0 to 6 with Sunday = 0.\\r\\nSetting `disabledDaysOfWeek` to `[]` clears the list and enables all days of the week.  \\r\\n\\r\\nGetting the `disabledDaysOfWeek` property returns the list of disabled days of the week set in the Editor or API.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** Setting `disabledDaysOfWeek` overrides any settings made in the Editor.\"},{\"name\":\"maxDate\",\"slug\":\"max-date\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's maximum date\",\"content\":\"let appointmentMaxDate = $w('#myAppointmentField').maxDate;\\n\\nlet maxStr = appointmentMaxDate.toDateString(); // 'Fri Feb 11 2022'\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's maximum date to today\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').maxDate = new Date();\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"DATE\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the latest date that a site visitor can select.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `maxDate` property prevents site visitors from selecting\\r\\ndates later than the specified maximum date.\\r\\n\\r\\nSet `maxDate` to `undefined` to remove the current maximum date limitation.\\r\\n\\r\\nGetting the `maxDate` property returns the current maximum\\r\\ndate that a site visitor can select.\"},{\"name\":\"minDate\",\"slug\":\"min-date\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's minimum date\",\"content\":\"let appointmentMinDate = $w('#myAppointmentField').minDate;\\n\\nlet minStr = appointmentMinDate.toDateString(); // \\\"Fri Jan 07 2022\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's minimum date to today\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').minDate = new Date();\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"DATE\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the earliest date that a site visitor can select.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `minDate` property prevents site visitors from selecting\\r\\ndates before the specified minimum date.\\r\\n\\r\\nSet `minDate` to `undefined` to remove the current minimum date limitation.\\r\\n\\r\\nGetting the `minDate` property returns the current minimum\\r\\ndate that a site visitor can select.\"},{\"name\":\"schedulingNotice\",\"slug\":\"scheduling-notice\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's schedulingNotice property\",\"content\":\"const schedulingNoticeHours = $w('#myAppointmentField').schedulingNotice; // 24\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's schedulingNotice property\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').schedulingNotice = 24;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the minimum amount of time before an appointment starts that a time slot is displayed.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `schedulingNotice` property sets the minimum number of hours before an appointment starts that it is displayed in the date and time elements. For example, by setting `schedulingNotice` to 12, only appointments that start 12 hours from now are displayed.\\r\\n\\r\\nGetting the `schedulingNotice` property returns the minimum number of hours before an appointment that its time slot is displayed.\\r\\n\\r\\n`schedulingNotice` can be set from 0 to 240 hours. Setting `schedulingNotice` to 0 displays all appointments.\"},{\"name\":\"timeIncrements\",\"slug\":\"time-increments\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's timeIncrements\",\"content\":\"const myIntervals = $w('#myAppointmentField').timeIncrements; // 30\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's timeIncrements\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').timeIncrements = 30;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Sets  or gets the interval between the times displayed in the time picker.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `timeIncrements` property sets the interval between the times displayed in the appointment field's time picker. For example setting `timeIncrements` to 15, displays selectable times with 15 minute intervals between them.\\r\\n\\r\\nGetting the `timeIncrements` property returns the interval between the times displayed in the appointment field's time picker.\\r\\n\\r\\nIncrements can be set from 1 to 60.\"},{\"name\":\"title\",\"slug\":\"title\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's title property\",\"content\":\"const appointmentFieldTitle = $w('#myAppointmentField').title;\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's title property\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').title = 'Select an appointment';\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the title of an appointment field.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn appointment field has a title that appears at the top of the field. Setting the `title` property sets the text that appears in the top section of the appointment field. Getting the `title` property gets the text that was set using the Editor or API.\"},{\"name\":\"useAmPmFormat\",\"slug\":\"use-am-pm-format\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's schedulingNotice property\",\"content\":\"const appointmentMinDate = $w('#myAppointmentField').useAmPmFormat;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's schedulingNotice property\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').useAmPmFormat = true;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the time format.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `useAmPmFormat` property to `true` sets the appointment field's time picker to a 12-hour format. Setting `useAmPmFormat` to `false` sets the time picker to a 24-hour format.\\r\\n\\r\\nGetting the `useAmPmFormat` property returns the current format for displaying the time.\"},{\"name\":\"value\",\"slug\":\"value\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's date amd time value and format it\",\"content\":\"const dateValue = $w('#myAppointmentField').value; // Thu Mar 31 2022 12:45:00 GMT-0500 (Eastern Standard Time)\\n\\nconst localeValue = dateValue.toLocaleDateString('en-US'); // 3/31/2022\\nconst stringValue = dateValue.toDateString(); // Thu Mar 31 2022\\nconst myTime = `${dateValue.getHours()}:${dateValue.getMinutes()}`;// 12:45\\nconst displayTimezone= dateValue.visitorTimeZone; // Asia/Tokyo\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's date and time value\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').value = new Date(\\\"2022-04-13T15:30-0500\\\");\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"DATE\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the date and time value of the appointment field.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `value` property sets the date and time displayed in the appointment field. \\r\\n Getting the `value` property gets the  appointment field's date and time according to the browser's locale and timezone.\\r\\n \\r\\n Set and get the timezone using the [`visitorTimeZone`](#visitorTimeZone) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n \u003e + Changing an appointment field's `value` in code doesn't trigger an `onChange` event.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + If an appointment field is connected to a dataset, setting the appointment field's `value`\\r\\n\u003e   in code doesn't set the value of the connected field in the dataset.\\r\\n\u003e   That means if you use the dataset to perform a submit, the value changed\\r\\n\u003e   in code isn't reflected in the submitted item.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + To submit the new value using a dataset, set the field's value using the\\r\\n\u003e   [`setFieldValue()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/set-field-value) function before\\r\\n\u003e   performing the submit.\"},{\"name\":\"visitorTimeZone\",\"slug\":\"visitor-time-zone\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an appointment field's visitorTimeZone property\",\"content\":\"let timeZone = $w('#myAppointmentField').visitorTimeZone;  // \\\"Pacific/Auckland\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set an appointment field's visitorTimeZone property\",\"content\":\"$w('#myAppointmentField').visitorTimeZone = 'Pacific/Auckland';\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the timezone dropdown value.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `visitorTimeZone` property sets the value in the timezone dropdown and updates the times in the time picker for the specified timezone. Use an [IANA timezone string ](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_tz_database_time_zones) to set the `visitorTimeZone` property. \\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the `visitorTimeZone` property returns the currently selected timezone from the timezone dropdown.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** The [`value`](#value) property always returns the date and time value according to the browser's timezone.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"valid\",\"slug\":\"valid\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether the element is valid\",\"content\":\"let isValid = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").valid; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an input element's value is valid.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `valid` property indicates if an element's value satisfies\\r\\n all conditions to pass a validation check. This includes basic validity\\r\\n conditions, such as whether the element has a value if it is `required`,\\r\\n and those specified in its [`onCustomValidation()`](#onCustomValidation)\\r\\n event handler, if you defined one.\\r\\n\\r\\n Note that validations other than **required**, including custom validations,\\r\\n are not run on input elements when they don't have a value.\"},{\"name\":\"validationMessage\",\"slug\":\"validation-message\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the validation message\",\"content\":\"let msg = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").validationMessage; // \\\"value missing\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets a message indicating why the element is invalid, or an\\r\\n empty string if the message is valid.\\r\\n\\r\\nSet the value of the `validationMessage` property using the\\r\\n `reject()` function of the [`onCustomValidation()`](#onCustomValidation)\\r\\n event handler.\"},{\"name\":\"validity\",\"slug\":\"validity\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Log ValidityState info\",\"content\":\"let validityObj = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").validity;\\n\\nlet customError = validityObj.customError;          // true\\nlet valid = validityObj.valid;                      // false\\nlet valueMissing = validityObj.valueMissing;        // false\\nlet typeMismatch = validityObj.typeMismatch;        // false\\nlet patternMismatch = validityObj.patternMismatch;  // false\\nlet tooLong = validityObj.tooLong;                  // false\\nlet tooShort = validityObj.tooShort;                // false\\nlet rangeUnderflow = validityObj.rangeUnderflow;    // false\\nlet rangeOverflow = validityObj.rangeOverflow;      // false\\nlet fileNotUploaded = validityObj.fileNotUploaded;  // false\\nlet stepMismatch = validityObj.stepMismatch;        // false\\nlet badInput = validityObj.badInput;                // false\\nlet invalidTime = validityObj.invalidTime;          // false\\nlet invalidDate = validityObj.invalidDate;          // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ValidityState\",\"referenceFqn\":\"ValidatableMixin.ValidityState\"},\"description\":\"Gets a ValidityState object that contains\\r\\n detailed information about the validity states of the element.\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"},{\"name\":\"enabled\",\"slug\":\"enabled\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's enabled status\",\"content\":\"let isEnabled = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled; // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is enabled or disabled.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `enabled` is `true`, users can interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `enabled` is `false`, users cannot interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n When an element is disabled:\\r\\n\\r\\n + Its color is faded or grayed out.\\r\\n + Animations that the element normally exhibits when being interacting\\r\\n   with do not occur.\\r\\n + Actions that the element has been configured to perform, such as\\r\\n   opening a link, do not occur.\\r\\n + Event handlers that have been bound to the element, such as with\\r\\n   `onMouseIn`, do not run.\\r\\n + If the element is an input element, such as a dropdown or text box,\\r\\n   users cannot interact with it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `enabled` property of an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`enable()`](#enable) or [`disable()`](#disable) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `enabled` property can also be set in the Editor using the Properties and Events panel.\"},{\"name\":\"required\",\"slug\":\"required\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set an element to be required\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").required = true;\"},{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is required\",\"content\":\"let isRequired = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").required; // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets whether an input element is required to have a value.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `required` property to `true` causes the\\r\\n element to be invalid if it\\r\\n doesn't contain a value. Setting it to false allows the element to be\\r\\n valid even if it doesn't contain a value. The validity of the element\\r\\n can be checked using its `validity`\\r\\n property.\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the value of the `required` property returns whether the element\\r\\n is required.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also set an input element to be required\\r\\n by using the element's Settings panel in the Editor.\"}]},{\"name\":\"AudioPlayer\",\"slug\":\"audio-player\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"mute\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.mute\",\"slug\":\"mute\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the volume has been muted.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Mute volume\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").mute();\"},{\"title\":\"Mute volume and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").mute()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with mute\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Mutes audio volume.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onEnded\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.onEnded\",\"slug\":\"on-ended\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"AudioPlayer\",\"referenceFqn\":\"AudioPlayer.AudioPlayer\",\"description\":\"The audio player that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the audio player whose audio track has ended\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").onEnded( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myAudioPlayer\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the audio track has ended.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when playback has ended.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn audio track ends when playback reaches the [`duration`](#duration) of the audio.\\r\\n\\r\\n If the audio track is set to play in a loop, this event handler is never triggered.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onPause\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.onPause\",\"slug\":\"on-pause\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"AudioPlayer\",\"referenceFqn\":\"AudioPlayer.AudioPlayer\",\"description\":\"The audio player that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the audio player that has been paused\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").onPause( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myAudioPlayer\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the audio track is paused.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when playback is paused.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn audio track can be paused by a user clicking the audio player's\\r\\n pause button or by calling its [`pause()`](#pause) or [`stop()`](#stop) functions.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onPlay\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.onPlay\",\"slug\":\"on-play\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"AudioPlayer\",\"referenceFqn\":\"AudioPlayer.AudioPlayer\",\"description\":\"The audio player that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the audio player that is playing\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").onPlay( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myAudioPlayer\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the audio track is played.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when playback is started or restarted.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn audio track can be played by a user clicking the audio player's\\r\\n play button or by calling its [`play()`](#play) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onProgress\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.onProgress\",\"slug\":\"on-progress\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"AudioPlayer\",\"referenceFqn\":\"AudioPlayer.AudioPlayer\",\"description\":\"The audio player that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the audio player whose audio track is progressing\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").onProgress( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myAudioPlayer\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the audio track progresses.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when playback progresses.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn audio track continually progresses as the audio plays.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"pause\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.pause\",\"slug\":\"pause\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When playback has been paused.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Pause playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").pause();\"},{\"title\":\"Pause playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").pause()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with pause\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Pauses playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `pause()` function pauses the audio track and fires a `pause` event.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `pause` event handlers set on the audio player by the [onPause( )](#onPause)\\r\\n function are called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"play\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.play\",\"slug\":\"play\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When playback begins or resumes.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Begin or resume playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").play();\"},{\"title\":\"Begin or resume playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").play()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with play\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Begins or resumes playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `play()` function plays the audio track and fires a `play` event.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `play` event handlers set on the audio player by the [onPlay( )](#onPlay)\\r\\n function are called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"seek\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.seek\",\"slug\":\"seek\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"time\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the playback has moved to the specified time.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Move playback to 1 minute and 42 seconds into the audio track\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").seek(102);\"},{\"title\":\"Move playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").seek(102)\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with seek\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"time\",\"slug\":\"time\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"The time to which to move the playback, in seconds.\"}],\"description\":\"Moves playback to the specified time, in seconds.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"stop\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.stop\",\"slug\":\"stop\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When playback has been stopped.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Stop playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").stop();\"},{\"title\":\"Stop playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").stop()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with stop\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Stops playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `stop()` function stops the playback, moves to the beginning\\r\\nof the audio track, and fires a `pause` event.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `pause` event handlers set on the audio player by the [onPause( )](#onPause)\\r\\n function are called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"togglePlay\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.togglePlay\",\"slug\":\"toggle-play\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When playback has been toggled.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Toggle playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").togglePlay();\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").togglePlay()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with toggle play\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Toggles playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `togglePlay()` function either pauses or plays the current playback based\\r\\n on its current state:\\r\\n\\r\\n + If the playback is paused, it plays and a `play` event is fired. The\\r\\n   `play` event handlers set on the audio player by the [onPlay( )](#onPlay)\\r\\n   function are called.\\r\\n + If the playback is playing, it is paused and a `pause` event is fired. The\\r\\n   `pause` event handlers set on the audio player by the [onPause( )](#onPause)\\r\\n   function are called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"unmute\",\"fqn\":\"AudioPlayer.unmute\",\"slug\":\"unmute\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the volume has been unmuted.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Unmute volume\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").unmute();\"},{\"title\":\"Unmute volume and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myAudioPlayer\\\").unmute()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with unmute\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Unmutes audio volume.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"ex