"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has entered the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportEnter( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has left the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportLeave( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Node.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo();\"},{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo()\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with scroll\\\");\\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nSetting the text property sets the plain-text contents of the text element. \\nAny text that the element already contained is replaced. The new text is \\nformatted using the formatting that was used on the first character of the previous text value.\\n\\nThe dashboard text element is intended for use on \\n[dashboard pages](https://dev.wix.com/docs/develop-websites/articles/coding-with-velo/frontend-code/dashboard-admin-pages/working-with-dashboard-pages) \\nin your Wix site or in [Wix Blocks](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-blocks-check-out-our-articles),\\nbut you may use it on any page.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"Note: This standard element property is not relevant for this DashboardText.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"text\",\"slug\":\"text\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dashboard text element's plain-text content\",\"content\":\"let dashboardText = $w('#myDashboardText').text;  // \\\"Some text\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text element's plain-text content\",\"content\":\"$w('#myDashboardText').text = \\\"Some text\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the plain-text contents of a text element.\\r\\n\\r\\nMax: 1200 characters\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is displayed on all pages\",\"content\":\"let isGlobal = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").global; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // \\\"page1\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").type; // \\\"$w.Type\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"}]},{\"name\":\"DashboardTextButton\",\"slug\":\"dashboard-text-button\",\"fqn\":\"DashboardTextButton\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"collapse\",\"fqn\":\"CollapsedMixin.collapse\",\"slug\":\"collapse\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Collapse an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\"},{\"title\":\"Collapse an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with collapse\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Collapses the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `collapse()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a collapsed element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also collapse an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `collapse()` function doesn't remove elements from the DOM. \\r\\n \u003e To soft delete an element from the DOM, use the `delete()` function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"expand\",\"fqn\":\"CollapsedMixin.expand\",\"slug\":\"expand\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Expand an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\"},{\"title\":\"Expand an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with expand\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Expands the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `expand()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an expanded element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, an element will not become visible by using `expand()` if it has been marked as \\\"Don't Display\\\" for the current breakpoint. Calling `expand()` will however, change the `collapsed` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e \\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `expand()` and `collapse()` with [**Hide**](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"hide\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenMixin.hide\",\"slug\":\"hide\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Hide an element with no effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\"},{\"title\":\"Hide an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide(\\\"fade\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Hide an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect and custom options\",\"content\":\"let fadeOptions = {\\n  \\\"duration\\\":   2000,\\n  \\\"delay\\\":      1000\\n};\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide(\\\"fade\\\", fadeOptions);\"},{\"title\":\"Hide an element with an effect and log a message when the effect is done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide(\\\"fade\\\")\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with fade\\\");\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when hiding the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Hides the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `true`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `hide()` function hides the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `hide()` function doesn't remove the element from the DOM.\\r\\n \u003e To temporarily delete an element from the DOM and prevent it from detection by SEO crawlers, \\r\\n use the `delete()` function.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a hidden element,\\r\\n see the `hidden` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when hiding the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n Effects:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"arc\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"bounce\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fade\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"flip\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"float\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fly\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fold\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"glide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"puff\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"roll\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"slide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"spin\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"turn\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"zoom\\\"`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also hide an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"show\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenMixin.show\",\"slug\":\"show\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Show an element with no effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect and custom options\",\"content\":\"let fadeOptions = {\\n  \\\"duration\\\":   2000,\\n  \\\"delay\\\":      1000\\n};\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\", fadeOptions);\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with an effect and log a message when the effect is done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\")\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with fade\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when showing the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when showing the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n This table shows possible `effectName` values\\r\\n and their corresponding names in the editor:\\r\\n\\r\\n | Effect Name Value    | Editor Animation Name |\\r\\n | -------------------- | -------------------------- |\\r\\n | `\\\"arc\\\"`              | Arc-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"bounce\\\"`           | Bounce-In                  |\\r\\n | `\\\"fade\\\"`             | Fade-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"flip\\\"`             | Flip-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"float\\\"`            | Float-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"fly\\\"`              | Fly-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"fold\\\"`             | Fold-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"glide\\\"`            | Glide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"puff\\\"`             | Puff-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"roll\\\"`             | Reveal                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"slide\\\"`            | Slide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"spin\\\"`             | Spin-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"turn\\\"`             | Turn-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"zoom\\\"`             | Expand-In                  |\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, the `show ()` function will not make an element visible for a given breakpoint\\r\\n\u003e   if the element has been set to \\\"**Hide** for that breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\\r\\n\u003e   Calling `show()` however, will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `show()` and `hide()` with **Hide** and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"disable\",\"fqn\":\"DisabledMixin.disable\",\"slug\":\"disable\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `enabled` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Disable an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\"},{\"title\":\"Disable an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Element now disabled\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Disables the element and sets its `enabled` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `disable()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's [`enabled`](#enabled) property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a disabled element,\\r\\n see the [`enabled`](#enabled) property.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"enable\",\"fqn\":\"DisabledMixin.enable\",\"slug\":\"enable\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `enabled` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Enable an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\"},{\"title\":\"Enable an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Element now enabled\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Enables the element and sets its `enabled` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `enable()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's [`enabled`](#enabled) property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an enabled element,\\r\\n see the [`enabled`](#enabled) property.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onClick\",\"slug\":\"on-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Change the background color of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').onClick((event) =\u003e {\\n  const clickedElement = event.target;\\n  clickedElement.style.backgroundColor = 'blue';\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `click` event when a user clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** To avoid unpredictable behavior, don't set redirect links in the editor for elements that already have an `onClick` event handler.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onDblClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onDblClick\",\"slug\":\"on-dbl-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was double-clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onDblClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is double-clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `dblClick` event when a user double-clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nA text button allows you to place text on your page that reacts when a visitor clicks on it.\\n\\nThe dashboard text button is intended for use on \\n[dashboard pages](https://dev.wix.com/docs/develop-websites/articles/coding-with-velo/frontend-code/dashboard-admin-pages/working-with-dashboard-pages) \\nin your Wix site or in [Wix Blocks](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-blocks-check-out-our-articles),\\nbut you may use it on any page.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"Note: This standard element property is not relevant for this DashboardTextButton.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"label\",\"slug\":\"label\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dashboard text button's label\",\"content\":\"let myLabel = $w('#myElement').label;  // \\\"Full Name\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button's label\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').label = \\\"Full Name\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Disable the dashboard text button's label\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').label = null; // Disables the element's label\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the button's label.\\r\\n\\r\\nMax: 1200 characters.\"},{\"name\":\"link\",\"slug\":\"link\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the URL a dashboard text button navigates to\",\"content\":\"let link = $w('#myElement').link; // https://wix.com\"},{\"title\":\"Set dashboard text button to open your site home page\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').link = \\\"/\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button to open an external web link in a new browser page when clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').link = \\\"http://wix.com\\\";\\n$w('#myElement').target = \\\"_blank\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button to open a document\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').link = \\\"wix:document://v1/9bec_52fb06ea/filename.xls\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button to open a new email window\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').link = \\\"mailto:user@example.com?subject=Some%20Topic\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button to make a phone call when clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').link = \\\"tel:+1-555-555-5555\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Disable the dashboard text button's target\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').link = null; // Disable the button's link property\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the dashboard text button's link.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen the dashboard text button is clicked, the browser navigates to the `link` location. \\r\\n\\r\\nYou can set `link` to any of the following:\\r\\n\\r\\n* `/localPageURL`: another page on your site\\r\\n* `/`: your site's home page\\r\\n* `http(s)://`: an external web address\\r\\n* `wix:document://`: a document stored in the Media Manager\\r\\n* `mailto:?subject=`: an email\\r\\n* `tel:`: a phone number\\r\\n\\r\\n The `link` property attempts to properly encode the URL value that\\r\\n you set. For example, `.../some page` is encoded to `.../some%20page`.\\r\\n However, some URLs do not have one unambiguous encoding. In those cases\\r\\n it is up to you to encode the URL to reflect your intentions. Because of\\r\\n these situations, it is a best practice to always encode URLs before you\\r\\n set them as the value of the `link` property. Regardless of how you set\\r\\n the `link` property, when you get its value, it returns an encoded URL.\\r\\n\\r\\n Note that Wix URLs do not contain spaces. A page which has spaces in its\\r\\n name has its spaces replaced with dashes (`-`). Similarly,\\r\\n a [dynamic page URL](https://support.wix.com/en/article/creating-a-unique-dynamic-page-url) which \\r\\n contains the value of a field in your collection with spaces\\r\\n has its spaces replaced with dashes (`-`).\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** Make sure to set your button link before running (and not inside) the [`onClick()`](/$w/dashboard-text-button/on-click) event handler.\"},{\"name\":\"prefix\",\"slug\":\"prefix\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dashboard text button prefix\",\"content\":\"let prefix = $w('#myInput').prefix; // $\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button prefix to a string literal\",\"content\":\"$w('#myInput').prefix = \\\"$\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button prefix to a vector image in the Media Manager\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').prefix = 'wix:vector://v1/ce0334_2cec984ab68c490891dda1b53a33fead.svg/my-vector-graphic.svg';\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button prefix to a vector XML string\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').prefix = '\u003csvg height=\\\"10\\\" width=\\\"10\\\"\u003e\u003cpolygon points=\\\"0,9 9,9 5,0\\\" style=\\\"fill:lime;stroke:purple;stroke-width:1\\\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e';\"},{\"title\":\"Disable the dashboard text button prefix\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').prefix = null; // Disable the button's prefix property\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the dashboard text button prefix.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can get or set a prefix for a dashboard text button. For example, you can set a prefix to be a \\r\\ncurrency, such as `'$'`.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThe following formats are supported:\\r\\n\\r\\n* A string literal, such as `'$'`.\\r\\n* Vector images from the Media Manager: `wix:vector://v1//`.\\r\\n* Vector images from the web: `http(s)://`.\\r\\n* Vector XML string: `...`.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo disable a text button's prefix, set the `prefix` property to `null`.\"},{\"name\":\"rel\",\"slug\":\"rel\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the link rel from a dashboard text button\",\"content\":\"let rel = $w('#myElement').rel; // \\\"noopener\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the link rel for a dashboard text button\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').rel = 'sponsored';\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the relationship between the page containing the dashboard text \\r\\nbutton link and the target page.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe dashboard text button's `rel` property provides additional context to search engines \\r\\nand browsers about how they should treat the link, influencing SEO, security, and \\r\\nother link behavior. \\r\\n\\r\\n Supported values:\\r\\n \\r\\n + `'noopener'`: Prevents the target page from accessing the source page with the\\r\\n[`window.opener`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/opener) property, \\r\\nreducing the risk of malicious code. \\r\\n + `'noreferrer'`: Prevents the browser from sending referrer information, such as the URL of \\r\\nthe source page, to the target page. This enhances user privacy by ensuring the target page can't \\r\\ntrack the origin of the visit.\\r\\n + `'nofollow'`: Tells search engines not to pass SEO link equity to the target page. This helps \\r\\nprevent the manipulation of search rankings and maintains the integrity of your site's SEO.\\r\\n + `'sponsored'`: Indicates that the link is part of a paid or promotional arrangement, \\r\\nensuring transparency and compliance with search engine guidelines.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Dashboard text buttons can have multiple `rel` values as a single string with each value separated by a space. \\r\\nFor example, `'nofollow sponsored'`. \\r\\n\\r\\n The default value for external web links (starting with `http://` and `https://`) is `'noopener'`.\"},{\"name\":\"suffix\",\"slug\":\"suffix\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dashboard text button suffix value\",\"content\":\"let prefix = $w('#myInput').suffix; // %\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button suffix value to a string literal\",\"content\":\"$w('#myInput').suffix = '%';\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button suffix to an vector image in the Media Manager\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').suffix = 'wix:vector://v1/ce0334_2cec984ab68c490891dda1b53a33fead.svg/my-vector-graphic.svg';\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button suffix to a vector XML string\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').suffix = '\u003csvg height=\\\"10\\\" width=\\\"10\\\"\u003e\u003cpolygon points=\\\"0,9 9,9 5,0\\\" style=\\\"fill:lime;stroke:purple;stroke-width:1\\\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e';\"},{\"title\":\"Disable the dashboard text button suffix\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').suffix = null; // Disable the button's suffix property\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the dashboard text button suffix.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can get or set a suffix for a dashboard text button. For example, you can set a suffix to be a \\r\\nunit of measurement, such as `'cm'`.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThe following formats are supported:\\r\\n\\r\\n* A string literal, such as `'cm'`.\\r\\n* Vector images from the Media Manager: `wix:vector://v1//`.\\r\\n* Vector images from the web: `http(s)://`.\\r\\n* Vector XML string: `...`.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo disable a text button suffix, set the `suffix` property to `null`.\"},{\"name\":\"target\",\"slug\":\"target\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dashboard text button's current target\",\"content\":\"let target = $w('#myElement').target; // \\\"_blank\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard text button's target\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').target = \\\"_self\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Reset the dashboard text button's target\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').target = null; // Resets the target property to its default value of \\\"_blank\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the target of the dashboard text button's link.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element's `target` determines where its [link](#link) opens. The\\r\\n target can be set so the [link](#link) opens in the current page or\\r\\n in a new page.\\r\\n\\r\\n Supported values are:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"_blank\\\"`: The link opens in a new tab or window.\\r\\n + `\\\"_self\\\"`: The link opens in the tab or window.\\r\\n + `null`: Resets the `target` property to its default value.\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"},{\"name\":\"enabled\",\"slug\":\"enabled\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's enabled status\",\"content\":\"let isEnabled = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled; // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is enabled or disabled.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `enabled` is `true`, users can interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `enabled` is `false`, users cannot interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n When an element is disabled:\\r\\n\\r\\n + Its color is faded or grayed out.\\r\\n + Animations that the element normally exhibits when being interacting\\r\\n   with do not occur.\\r\\n + Actions that the element has been configured to perform, such as\\r\\n   opening a link, do not occur.\\r\\n + Event handlers that have been bound to the element, such as with\\r\\n   `onMouseIn`, do not run.\\r\\n + If the element is an input element, such as a dropdown or text box,\\r\\n   users cannot interact with it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `enabled` property of an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`enable()`](#enable) or [`disable()`](#disable) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `enabled` property can also be set in the Editor using the Properties and Events panel.\"}]},{\"name\":\"DashboardToggleSwitch\",\"slug\":\"dashboard-toggle-switch\",\"fqn\":\"DashboardToggleSwitch\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"collapse\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.collapse\",\"slug\":\"collapse\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"description\":\"Collapses the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `collapse()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a collapsed element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also collapse an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `collapse()` function doesn't remove elements from the DOM. \\r\\n \u003e To soft delete an element from the DOM, use the `delete()` function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"expand\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.expand\",\"slug\":\"expand\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"description\":\"Expands the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `expand()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an expanded element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, an element will not become visible by using `expand()` if it has been marked as \\\"Don't Display\\\" for the current breakpoint. Calling `expand()` will however, change the `collapsed` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e \\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `expand()` and `collapse()` with [**Hide**](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"hide\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.hide\",\"slug\":\"hide\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when hiding the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Hides the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `true`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `hide()` function hides the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `hide()` function doesn't remove the element from the DOM.\\r\\n \u003e To temporarily delete an element from the DOM and prevent it from detection by SEO crawlers, \\r\\n use the `delete()` function.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a hidden element,\\r\\n see the `hidden` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when hiding the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n Effects:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"arc\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"bounce\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fade\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"flip\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"float\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fly\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fold\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"glide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"puff\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"roll\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"slide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"spin\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"turn\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"zoom\\\"`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also hide an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse enters an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseIn( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved onto the\\r\\n element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n onto the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseOut\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseOut\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-out\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse exits an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseOut( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved off of\\r\\n the element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n off of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportEnter\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onViewportEnter\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-enter\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Element.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"show\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.show\",\"slug\":\"show\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when showing the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when showing the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n This table shows possible `effectName` values\\r\\n and their corresponding names in the editor:\\r\\n\\r\\n | Effect Name Value    | Editor Animation Name |\\r\\n | -------------------- | -------------------------- |\\r\\n | `\\\"arc\\\"`              | Arc-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"bounce\\\"`           | Bounce-In                  |\\r\\n | `\\\"fade\\\"`             | Fade-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"flip\\\"`             | Flip-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"float\\\"`            | Float-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"fly\\\"`              | Fly-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"fold\\\"`             | Fold-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"glide\\\"`            | Glide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"puff\\\"`             | Puff-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"roll\\\"`             | Reveal                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"slide\\\"`            | Slide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"spin\\\"`             | Spin-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"turn\\\"`             | Turn-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"zoom\\\"`             | Expand-In                  |\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, the `show ()` function will not make an element visible for a given breakpoint\\r\\n\u003e   if the element has been set to \\\"**Hide** for that breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\\r\\n\u003e   Calling `show()` however, will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `show()` and `hide()` with **Hide** and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"disable\",\"fqn\":\"DisabledMixin.disable\",\"slug\":\"disable\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `enabled` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Disable an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\"},{\"title\":\"Disable an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Element now disabled\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Disables the element and sets its `enabled` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `disable()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's [`enabled`](#enabled) property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a disabled element,\\r\\n see the [`enabled`](#enabled) property.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"enable\",\"fqn\":\"DisabledMixin.enable\",\"slug\":\"enable\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `enabled` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Enable an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\"},{\"title\":\"Enable an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Element now enabled\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Enables the element and sets its `enabled` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `enable()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's [`enabled`](#enabled) property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an enabled element,\\r\\n see the [`enabled`](#enabled) property.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nThe dashboard toggle switch is intended for use on \\n[dashboard pages](https://dev.wix.com/docs/develop-websites/articles/coding-with-velo/frontend-code/dashboard-admin-pages/working-with-dashboard-pages) \\nin your Wix site or in [Wix Blocks](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-blocks-check-out-our-articles),\\nbut you may use it on any page.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"checked\",\"slug\":\"checked\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether the dashboard toggle switch is on\",\"content\":\"let isChecked = $w('#mySwitch').checked;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard toggle switch on\",\"content\":\"$w('#mySwitch').checked = true;\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dasbhoard toggle switch off\",\"content\":\"$w('#mySwitch').checked = false;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the state of the toggle switch.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `checked` property to `true` turns the toggle switch on. Setting it to `false` turns the toggle switch off.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"Note: This standard element property is not relevant for this DashboardToggleSwitch.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"label\",\"slug\":\"label\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dashboard toggle switch label\",\"content\":\"let myLabel = $w('#myElement').label;  // \\\"Full Name\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard toggle switch label\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').label = \\\"Full Name\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Disable the dashboard toggle switch label\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').label = null; // Disables the element's label\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the toggle switch label.\\r\\n\\r\\nMax: 120 characters\"},{\"name\":\"tooltip\",\"slug\":\"tooltip\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dashboard toggle switch's tooltip text\",\"content\":\"let tooltip = $w('#myElement').tooltip; // \\\"Submit your information here\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the dashboard toggle switch's tooltip text\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').tooltip = \\\"Submit your information here\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Disable the dashboard toggle switch's tooltip\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').tooltip = null; // Disables the tooltip\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the toggle switch's tooltip content.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `tooltip` property defines the text that is displayed when a visitor hovers over an element's ![tooltip-icon](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_tooltip-icon.png) icon.\\r\\nSet `tooltip` to `null` to disable.\\r\\n\\r\\nMax: 1200 characters\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"enabled\",\"slug\":\"enabled\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's enabled status\",\"content\":\"let isEnabled = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled; // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is enabled or disabled.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `enabled` is `true`, users can interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `enabled` is `false`, users cannot interact with the element.\\r\\n\\r\\n When an element is disabled:\\r\\n\\r\\n + Its color is faded or grayed out.\\r\\n + Animations that the element normally exhibits when being interacting\\r\\n   with do not occur.\\r\\n + Actions that the element has been configured to perform, such as\\r\\n   opening a link, do not occur.\\r\\n + Event handlers that have been bound to the element, such as with\\r\\n   `onMouseIn`, do not run.\\r\\n + If the element is an input element, such as a dropdown or text box,\\r\\n   users cannot interact with it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `enabled` property of an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`enable()`](#enable) or [`disable()`](#disable) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `enabled` property can also be set in the Editor using the Properties and Events panel.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Dataset\",\"slug\":\"dataset\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"add\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset.add\",\"slug\":\"add\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When a new empty item is the current item of the dataset.\\r\\nRejected - An error message.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Save the current item and add a new blank item\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").add()\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"New item added\\\");\\n  } )\\n  .catch( (err) =\u003e {\\n    let errMsg = err;\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Save the current item and add a new blank item when the page loads\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady( () =\u003e {\\n  $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").onReady( () =\u003e {\\n    $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").add()\\n      .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n        console.log(\\\"New item added\\\");\\n      } )\\n      .catch( (err) =\u003e {\\n        let errMsg = err;\\n      } );\\n\\n  } );\\n  \\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Adds a new blank item.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `add()` function saves the current item and then adds a new blank\\r\\n item. When the editing of the new item is complete, you will need to\\r\\n call another function that will save the new item.\\r\\n\\r\\n The index of the new item is one after the index of the current item, or\\r\\n zero if there is no current item.\\r\\n\\r\\n Note that since the `add()` function begins by saving the current item,\\r\\n if the current item cannot be saved for any reason, such as it does not\\r\\n pass validation, calling the function will cause an error.\\r\\n\\r\\n Calling `add()` on a read-only dataset causes an error.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e A dataset needs to load its data before you call its `add()` function.\\r\\n \u003e Usually a dataset finishes loading a short time after the page it is on finishes\\r\\n \u003e loading. So if you call `add()` inside the page’s [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler, the dataset might not be ready yet.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e To call `add()` as soon as possible after a page loads, use the **dataset's**\\r\\n \u003e [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/on-ready) function inside the **page’s** [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler to ensure that both the page and the dataset have finished loading.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e This function replaces the deprecated [`new()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/new) function. The deprecated function will continue to work, but will not receive updates.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"getCurrentItem\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset.getCurrentItem\",\"slug\":\"get-current-item\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"object\",\"description\":\"The current item, or null if there is no current item.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the dataset's current item\",\"content\":\"let itemObj = $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getCurrentItem();\\n\\n/*  \\n *  {\\n *    \\\"_id\\\":                \\\"fcec780a-3e37-4b64-8a66-37c552c53f99\\\",\\n *    \\\"_owner\\\":             \\\"f6c0f9c3-a62d-7e9f-g58d-943829af244d9\\\",\\n *    \\\"_createdDate\\\":       \\\"2017-05-01T17:19:03.823Z\\\",\\n *    \\\"_updatedDate\\\":       \\\"2017-05-01T17:19:10.477Z\\\",\\n *    \\\"title\\\":              \\\"Dr. \\\",\\n *    \\\"name\\\":               \\\"B\\\",\\n *    \\\"link-dynamic-name\\\":  \\\"/myCollection/B\\\"\\n *  }\\n */\"},{\"title\":\"Get the dataset's current item when the page loads\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady( () =\u003e {\\n  $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").onReady( () =\u003e {\\n    let itemObj = $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getCurrentItem();\\n\\n  } );\\n\\n} );\\n\\n/*  itemObj:\\n *\\n *  {\\n *    \\\"_id\\\":                \\\"fcec780a-3e37-4b64-8a66-37c552c53f99\\\",\\n *    \\\"_owner\\\":             \\\"f6c0f9c3-a62d-7e9f-g58d-943829af244d9\\\",\\n *    \\\"_createdDate\\\":       \\\"2017-05-01T17:19:03.823Z\\\",\\n *    \\\"_updatedDate\\\":       \\\"2017-05-01T17:19:10.477Z\\\",\\n *    \\\"title\\\":              \\\"Dr. \\\",\\n *    \\\"name\\\":               \\\"B\\\",\\n *    \\\"link-dynamic-name\\\":  \\\"/myCollection/B\\\"\\n *  }\\n */\"},{\"title\":\"Get the dataset's current item when an item is clicked in a repeater\",\"description\":\"This example demonstrates how to get an item's details using the `at()` function. We use this\\n function to establish context when a repeater container is clicked.\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady( function () {\\n  $w(\\\"#repeatedContainer\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n    let $item = $w.at(event.context);\\n    let clickedItemData = $item(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getCurrentItem();\\n  } );\\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Returns the current item.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `getCurrentItem()` function returns an object whose key:value pairs\\r\\n are the field IDs and field values of the current item, including all\\r\\n hidden fields. Fields that do not have a value are omitted from the\\r\\n returned object.\\r\\n\\r\\n When called on a write-only or read \u0026 write dataset,\\r\\n `getCurrentItem()` returns the unsaved state of the current item.\\r\\n\\r\\n Returns `null` or `undefined` if the dataset:\\r\\n\\r\\n + Is filtered to not match any items in the collection.\\r\\n + Is empty.\\r\\n + Has not loaded yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:**\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e A dataset needs to load its data before you call its `getCurrentItem()` function.\\r\\n \u003e  Usually a dataset finishes loading a short time after the page it is on finishes\\r\\n \u003e loading. So if you call `getCurrentItem()` inside the page’s [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler, the dataset might not be ready yet.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e To call `getCurrentItem()` as soon as possible after a page loads, use the **dataset's**\\r\\n \u003e [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/on-ready) function inside the **page’s** [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler to ensure that both the page and the dataset have finished loading.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e If the current item is changed from a non-dataset source, such as by\\r\\n \u003e selecting a row in a table connected to a dataset or clicking a button set\\r\\n \u003e to advance to the next item in a dataset, the dataset's current item is\\r\\n \u003e not updated immediately. Therefore, to get the dataset's new current item,\\r\\n \u003e call `getCurrentItem()` in the dataset's [`onCurrentIndexChanged()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/on-current-index-changed)\\r\\n \u003e event handler. Do not use the events of the non-dataset source, such as\\r\\n \u003e [`onRowSelect`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/table/on-row-select) or `onClick`,\\r\\n \u003e to call `getCurrentItem()` because they will fire before the dataset's\\r\\n \u003e current item is updated.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"getCurrentItemIndex\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset.getCurrentItemIndex\",\"slug\":\"get-current-item-index\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The index of the current item, or null if there is no current item.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the current item's index\",\"content\":\"let itemIndex = $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getCurrentItemIndex(); // 3\"}],\"description\":\"Returns the current item's index.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `getCurrentItemIndex()` function returns the index of current item\\r\\n within the items of the dataset. The indices of the items in a dataset\\r\\n are zero-based. For example, if the third item is the current item, then\\r\\n `getCurrentItemIndex()` returns `2`.\\r\\n\\r\\n Calling `getCurrentItemIndex()` on a write-only dataset causes an error.\\r\\n\\r\\n Returns `null` if one of the following is true if the dataset:\\r\\n\\r\\n + Is filtered to not match any items in the collection.\\r\\n + Is empty.\\r\\n + Has not loaded yet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:**\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e A dataset needs to load its data before you call its `getCurrentItemIndex()` function.\\r\\n\u003e Usually a dataset finishes loading a short time after the page it is on finishes\\r\\n\u003e  loading. So if you call `getCurrentItemIndex()` inside the page’s [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n\u003e event handler, the dataset might not be ready yet.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e To call `getCurrentItemIndex()` as soon as possible after a page loads, use the **dataset's**\\r\\n \u003e [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/on-ready) function inside the **page’s** [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler to ensure that both the page and the dataset have finished loading.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e If the current item is changed from a non-dataset source, such as by\\r\\n \u003e selecting a row in a table connected to a dataset or clicking a button set\\r\\n \u003e to advance to the next item in a dataset, the dataset's current item is\\r\\n \u003e not updated immediately. Therefore, to get the dataset's new current item index,\\r\\n \u003e call `getCurrentItemIndex()` in the dataset's [`onCurrentIndexChanged()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/on-current-index-changed)\\r\\n \u003e event handler. Do not use the events of the non-dataset source, such as\\r\\n \u003e [`onRowSelect`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/table/on-row-select) or `onClick`,\\r\\n \u003e to call `getCurrentItemIndex()` because they will fire before the dataset's\\r\\n \u003e current item is updated.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"getCurrentPageIndex\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset.getCurrentPageIndex\",\"slug\":\"get-current-page-index\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The index of the current page or null if there is no current page.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the current page's index\",\"content\":\"let pageCount = $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getCurrentPageIndex(); // 1\"}],\"description\":\"Gets the index of the dataset's current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `getCurrentPageIndex()` function returns the index of current dataset\\r\\n [page](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/introduction#dataset-pages). The indices of the dataset's pages start at `1`.\\r\\n \u003e **Note:**\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e A dataset needs to load its data before you call its `getCurrentPageIndex()` function.\\r\\n \u003e Usually a dataset finishes loading a short time after the page it is on finishes\\r\\n \u003e loading. So if you call `getCurrentPageIndex()` inside the page’s [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler, the dataset might not be ready yet.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e To call `getCurrentPageIndex()` as soon as possible after a page loads, use the **dataset's**\\r\\n \u003e [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/on-ready) function inside the **page’s** [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler to ensure that both the page and the dataset have finished loading.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"getItems\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset.getItems\",\"slug\":\"get-items\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"fromIndex\",\"numberOfItems\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GetItemsResult\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Dataset.GetItemsResult\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - The items retrieved and the total number of items in the dataset that match its filter criteria.\\r\\nRejected - An error object.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get items from the dataset\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getItems(3, 2)\\n  .then( (result) =\u003e {\\n    let items = result.items;\\n    let totalCount = result.totalCount;\\n    let offset = result.offset;\\n  } )\\n  .catch( (err) =\u003e {\\n    let errMsg = err.message;\\n    let errCode = err.code;\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Get items from the dataset when the page loads\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady( () =\u003e {\\n  $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").onReady( () =\u003e {\\n    $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getItems(3, 2)\\n      .then( (result) =\u003e {\\n        let items = result.items;\\n        let totalCount = result.totalCount;\\n        let offset = result.offset;\\n      } )\\n      .catch( (err) =\u003e {\\n        let errMsg = err.message;\\n        let errCode = err.code;\\n      } );\\n\\n  } );\\n\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"fromIndex\",\"slug\":\"from-index\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"The index of the first item to return.\"},{\"name\":\"numberOfItems\",\"slug\":\"number-of-items\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"The number of items to return.\"}],\"description\":\"Returns the selected items.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `getItems()` function returns a Promise that is resolved to\\r\\n a `GetItemsResult` object when the items have been\\r\\n retrieved.\\r\\n\\r\\n Calling `getItems()` on a write-only dataset causes an error.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:**\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e A dataset needs to load its data before you call its `getItems()` function.\\r\\n \u003e Usually a dataset finishes loading a short time after the page it is on finishes\\r\\n \u003e loading. So if you call `getItems()` inside the page’s [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler, the dataset might not be ready yet.\\r\\n \u003e\\r\\n \u003e To call `getItems()` as soon as possible after a page loads, use the **dataset's**\\r\\n \u003e [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/on-ready) function inside the **page’s** [`onReady()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/on-ready)\\r\\n \u003e event handler to ensure that both the page and the dataset have finished loading.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"getPageSize\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset.getPageSize\",\"slug\":\"get-page-size\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\",\"description\":\"The page size.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the current page size\",\"content\":\"let pageSize = $w(\\\"#myDataset\\\").getPageSize(); // 6\"}],\"description\":\"Gets the dataset's page size.\\r\\n\\r\\nGets the current [page](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/introduction#dataset-pages) size set in the Editor or using the\\r\\n [`setPageSize`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/set-page-size) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"getTotalCount\",\"fqn\":\"Dataset.getTotalCount\",\"slug\":\"get-total-count\",\"i