; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has left the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportLeave( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Node.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo();\"},{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo()\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with scroll\\\");\\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onClick\",\"slug\":\"on-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Change the background color of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').onClick((event) =\u003e {\\n  const clickedElement = event.target;\\n  clickedElement.style.backgroundColor = 'blue';\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `click` event when a user clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** To avoid unpredictable behavior, don't set redirect links in the editor for elements that already have an `onClick` event handler.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onDblClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onDblClick\",\"slug\":\"on-dbl-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was double-clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onDblClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is double-clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `dblClick` event when a user double-clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\n\u003e**Note:** This API is not available in Wix Editor.\\n\\nThe [hamburger menu](https://support.wix.com/en/article/editor-x-using-hamburger-menus) \\nis a compact navigational component used to save space on your site.\\nRepresented by an icon and usually positioned in the corner \\nof a site, the menu remains hidden until the user clicks on the icon. This activates\\nthe hamburger menu container to expand and reveal the menu items.\\n\\nThe hamburger menu container consists of a list of links that guide the \\nuser to pages on your site. It also includes a fullscreen overlay and a close button,\\nwhich users can click to collapse the menu back to its hidden state.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"},{\"content\":\"\u003c!-- This article was published using the Doc Push single-sourcing tool. Any changes to this article MUST be made in the source file. Find it at www.github.com/wix-private/velo-docs.--\u003e\\n\\n# Hamburger Menu Container CSS Classes\\n\\n\u003e This feature is only available to Wix Studio users.\\n\\nYou can use the classes listed below\\nto style your `HamburgerMenuContainer` elements with CSS.\\n\\nFor more information on styling your elements with CSS, see\\n[Styling Elements with CSS]($w/styling-elements-with-css) and the\\n[MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\\n\\n\u003cblockquote class=\\\"important\\\"\u003e\\n\\n__Important:__\\nElement structure and undocumented class names\\nmay change without advance warning.\\nTo avoid unintended style changes to your site,\\nselect elements with the documented class names only.\\n\\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\\n\\n## `.hamburger-menu-container`\\n\\nTargets `hamburgerMenuContainer` item.\\nFor example:\\n\\n```css\\n.hamburger-menu-container {\\n  width: 50%;\\n  height: 70%;\\n  background-color: #92f0a0;\\n}\\n```\\n\",\"displayName\":\"CSS Classes\",\"slugifyName\":\"css-classes\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"opened\",\"slug\":\"opened\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Indicates if the menu container is currently open\",\"content\":\"if($w(\\\"#myMenuContainer\\\").opened) {\\n    $w(\\\"#myMenuContainer\\\").close();\\n  }\\n  else {\\n    $w(\\\"#myMenuContainer\\\").open();\\n  }\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the hamburger menu container is currently open.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `opened` is `true`, the container is visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `opened` is `false` the container is hidden.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is displayed on all pages\",\"content\":\"let isGlobal = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").global; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // \\\"page1\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").type; // \\\"$w.Type\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"children\",\"slug\":\"children\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's children\",\"content\":\"let myChildren = $w(\\\"#myContainer\\\").children;\\n\\nlet firstChild = myChildren[0];\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\"}},\"description\":\"Gets an array of the elements that are contained within the element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements, such as pages, headers, footers, and boxes, can contain\\r\\n other elements. This occurs when you drag an element onto a container\\r\\n element and [attach it](https://www.wix.com/support/html5/article/attaching-elements-to-a-box).\\r\\n These attached elements are considered the parent element's children.\"}]},{\"name\":\"HamburgerOpenButton\",\"slug\":\"hamburger-open-button\",\"fqn\":\"HamburgerOpenButton\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"onClick\",\"fqn\":\"HamburgerOpenButton.onClick\",\"slug\":\"on-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myButton\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n    let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myButton\\\"\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myButton\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n    let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n    let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n    let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n    let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n    let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n    let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n    let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n    let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Change the background of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myButton').onClick((event) =\u003e {\\n    const clickedElement = event.target;\\n    clickedElement.style.backgroundColor = 'blue';\\n  });\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `click` event when user clicks on the element and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** Do not use the Editor Link panel to redirect on click when a link is already \\r\\n defined using the `onClick()` function. To avoid unpredictable behavior, remove \\r\\n the link from the Editor Link panel.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse enters an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseIn( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved onto the\\r\\n element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n onto the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseOut\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseOut\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-out\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse exits an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseOut( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved off of\\r\\n the element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n off of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportEnter\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportEnter\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-enter\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has entered the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportEnter( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has left the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportLeave( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Node.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo();\"},{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo()\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with scroll\\\");\\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"collapse\",\"fqn\":\"CollapsedMixin.collapse\",\"slug\":\"collapse\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Collapse an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\"},{\"title\":\"Collapse an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with collapse\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Collapses the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `collapse()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a collapsed element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also collapse an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `collapse()` function doesn't remove elements from the DOM. \\r\\n \u003e To soft delete an element from the DOM, use the `delete()` function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"expand\",\"fqn\":\"CollapsedMixin.expand\",\"slug\":\"expand\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Expand an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\"},{\"title\":\"Expand an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with expand\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Expands the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `expand()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an expanded element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, an element will not become visible by using `expand()` if it has been marked as \\\"Don't Display\\\" for the current breakpoint. Calling `expand()` will however, change the `collapsed` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e \\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `expand()` and `collapse()` with [**Hide**](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"hide\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenMixin.hide\",\"slug\":\"hide\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Hide an element with no effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\"},{\"title\":\"Hide an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide(\\\"fade\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Hide an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect and custom options\",\"content\":\"let fadeOptions = {\\n  \\\"duration\\\":   2000,\\n  \\\"delay\\\":      1000\\n};\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide(\\\"fade\\\", fadeOptions);\"},{\"title\":\"Hide an element with an effect and log a message when the effect is done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide(\\\"fade\\\")\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with fade\\\");\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when hiding the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Hides the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `true`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `hide()` function hides the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `hide()` function doesn't remove the element from the DOM.\\r\\n \u003e To temporarily delete an element from the DOM and prevent it from detection by SEO crawlers, \\r\\n use the `delete()` function.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a hidden element,\\r\\n see the `hidden` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when hiding the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n Effects:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"arc\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"bounce\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fade\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"flip\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"float\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fly\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fold\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"glide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"puff\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"roll\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"slide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"spin\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"turn\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"zoom\\\"`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also hide an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"show\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenMixin.show\",\"slug\":\"show\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Show an element with no effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect and custom options\",\"content\":\"let fadeOptions = {\\n  \\\"duration\\\":   2000,\\n  \\\"delay\\\":      1000\\n};\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\", fadeOptions);\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with an effect and log a message when the effect is done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\")\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with fade\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when showing the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when showing the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n This table shows possible `effectName` values\\r\\n and their corresponding names in the editor:\\r\\n\\r\\n | Effect Name Value    | Editor Animation Name |\\r\\n | -------------------- | -------------------------- |\\r\\n | `\\\"arc\\\"`              | Arc-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"bounce\\\"`           | Bounce-In                  |\\r\\n | `\\\"fade\\\"`             | Fade-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"flip\\\"`             | Flip-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"float\\\"`            | Float-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"fly\\\"`              | Fly-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"fold\\\"`             | Fold-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"glide\\\"`            | Glide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"puff\\\"`             | Puff-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"roll\\\"`             | Reveal                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"slide\\\"`            | Slide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"spin\\\"`             | Spin-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"turn\\\"`             | Turn-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"zoom\\\"`             | Expand-In                  |\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, the `show ()` function will not make an element visible for a given breakpoint\\r\\n\u003e   if the element has been set to \\\"**Hide** for that breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\\r\\n\u003e   Calling `show()` however, will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `show()` and `hide()` with **Hide** and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\n\u003e**Note:** This API is not available in Wix Editor.\\n\\nA vector image used as the icon for the hamburger open button. \\nWhen the users clicks the icon the hamburger menu container opens.\\n\\nThe following formats are supported:\\n+ Vector images from the Media Manager: `wix:vector://v1/\u003cvector_uri\u003e/\u003cfilename\u003e`\\n+ Vector images from the web: `http(s)://\u003cvector image url\u003e`\\n+ Vector XML string: `\u003csvg\u003e...\u003c/svg\u003e`\\n\\n\u003e**Note:** [Image Buttons](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-adding-and-setting-up-an-image-button) don't support this property.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"},{\"content\":\"\u003c!-- This article was published using the Doc Push single-sourcing tool. Any changes to this article MUST be made in the source file. Find it at www.github.com/wix-private/velo-docs.--\u003e\\n\\n# Hamburger Open Button CSS Classes\\n\\n\u003e This feature is only available to Wix Studio users.\\n\\nYou can use the classes listed below\\nto style your `HamburgerOpen` elements with CSS.\\n\\nFor more information on styling your elements with CSS, see\\n[Styling Elements with CSS]($w/styling-elements-with-css) and the\\n[MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\\n\\n\u003cblockquote class=\\\"important\\\"\u003e\\n\\n__Important:__\\nElement structure and undocumented class names\\nmay change without advance warning.\\nTo avoid unintended style changes to your site,\\nselect elements with the documented class names only.\\n\\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\\n\\n## `.hamburger-open-button`\\n\\nTargets `hamburgerOpenButton` element.\\nFor example:\\n\\n```css\\n.hamburger-open-button {\\n  width: 90%;\\n  cursor: default;\\n  background-color: #116dff;\\n}\\n```\\n## `.hamburger-open-button__label`\\n\\nTargets `hamburgerOpenButton` [label text]($w/button/label).\\nFor example:\\n\\n```css\\n.hamburger-open-button__label {\\n  font-family: sans-serif;\\n  font-weight: 700;\\n  text-transform: lowercase;\\n  color: black;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## `.hamburger-open-button__icon `\\n\\nTargets `hamburgerOpenButton` [icon images]($w/button/icon).\\nFor example:\\n\\n```css\\n.hamburger-open-button__icon {\\n  width: 20px;\\n  height: 40px;\\n  border-radius: 20%;\\n  box-shadow: 5px 5px 5px;\\n}\\n```\\n\",\"displayName\":\"CSS Classes\",\"slugifyName\":\"css-classes\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"icon\",\"slug\":\"icon\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set a button's icon to a Media Manager image\",\"content\":\"$w('#myButton').icon = 'wix:vector://v1/ce0334_2cec984ab68c490891dda1b53a33fead.svg/my-vector-graphic.svg';\"},{\"title\":\"Set a button's icon to an XML string\",\"content\":\"$w('#myButton').icon = '\u003csvg height=\\\"10\\\" width=\\\"10\\\"\u003e\u003cpolygon points=\\\"0,9 9,9 5,0\\\" style=\\\"fill:lime;stroke:purple;stroke-width:1\\\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e';\"},{\"title\":\"Delete a button's icon\",\"content\":\"$w('#myButton').icon = '';\"},{\"title\":\"Get a button's icon\",\"content\":\"let iconLocation = $w('#myButton').icon;\\n// 'wix:vector://v1/ce0334_2cec984ab68c490891dda1b53a33fead.svg/my-vector-graphic.svg'\"},{\"title\":\"Change a button's icon when a site visitor clicks the button\",\"content\":\"$w('#myButton').onClick((event) =\u003e {\\n    $w('#myButton').icon = 'wix:vector://v1/ce0334_2cec984ab68c490891dda1b53a33fead.svg/my-vector-graphic.svg';\\n});\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the icon image displayed on the button.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `icon` property defines the vector image used as the button's icon.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting `icon` changes the button icon to the image indicated by the new value.\\r\\nGetting the `icon` property returns the location of the icon image file.\\r\\nTo delete a button's icon set `icon` to `null`, `undefined`, or an empty string.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following formats are supported:\\r\\n + Vector images from the Media Manager: `wix:vector://v1//`\\r\\n + Vector images from the web: `http(s)://`\\r\\n + Vector XML string: `...`\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** [Image Buttons](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-adding-and-setting-up-an-image-button) are not supported by the `HamburgerCloseButton`.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is displayed on all pages\",\"content\":\"let isGlobal = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").global; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // \\\"page1\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").type; // \\\"$w.Type\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"},{\"name\":\"style\",\"slug\":\"style\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set the background color\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").style.backgroundColor = \\\"rgba(255,0,0,0.5)\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Get the background color\",\"content\":\"let bgColor = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").style.backgroundColor;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Style\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Style.Style\"},\"description\":\"Gets an object containing information about the element's styles.\"},{\"name\":\"label\",\"slug\":\"label\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's label\",\"content\":\"let label = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").label;  // \\\"Submit\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set an element's label\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").label = \\\"New Label\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the label of an element.\"},{\"name\":\"effects\",\"slug\":\"effects\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's effects\",\"content\":\"let myEffects = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").effects;\\n\\nlet firstEffect = myEffects[0];\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Effects\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Effects.Effects\"},\"description\":\"An object containing functionality for displaying the [effects](https://support.wix.com/en/article/studio-editor-adding-a-preset-click-or-hover-interaction) defined for an element using Wix Studio.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** This API can only be used in Wix Studio.\"}]},{\"name\":\"HamburgerOverlay\",\"slug\":\"hamburger-overlay\",\"fqn\":\"HamburgerOverlay\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse enters an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseIn( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved onto the\\r\\n element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n onto the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseOut\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseOut\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-out\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse exits an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseOut( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved off of\\r\\n the element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n off of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportEnter\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportEnter\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-enter\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has entered the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportEnter( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has left the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportLeave( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Node.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo();\"},{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo()\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with scroll\\\");\\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onClick\",\"slug\":\"on-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Change the background color of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').onClick((event) =\u003e {\\n  const clickedElement = event.target;\\n  clickedElement.style.backgroundColor = 'blue';\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `click` event when a user clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** To avoid unpredictable behavior, don't set redirect links in the editor for elements that already have an `onClick` event handler.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onDblClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onDblClick\",\"slug\":\"on-dbl-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was double-clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onDblClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is double-clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `dblClick` event when a user double-clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\n\u003e **Note:** This API is not available in Wix Editor.\\n\\nThe hamburger overlay is a visual component, which appears as a dark layer beneath the\\nhamburger menu container. The overlay displays when the hamburger menu container is open.\\nIts function is to direct user attention towards the menu items for improved navigation.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"},{\"content\":\"\u003c!-- This article was published using the Doc Push single-sourcing tool. Any changes to this article MUST be made in the source file. Find it at www.github.com/wix-private/velo-docs.--\u003e\\n\\n# Hamburger Overlay CSS Classes\\n\\n\u003e This feature is only available to Wix Studio users.\\n\\nYou can use the classes listed below\\nto style your `HamburgerOverlay` elements with CSS.\\n\\nFor more information on styling your elements with CSS, see\\n[Styling Elements with CSS]($w/styling-elements-with-css) and the\\n[MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\\n\\n\u003cblockquote class=\\\"important\\\"\u003e\\n\\n__Important:__\\nElement structure and undocumented class names\\nmay change without advance warning.\\nTo avoid unintended style changes to your site,\\nselect elements with the documented class names only.\\n\\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\\n\\n## `.hamburger-overlay`\\n\\nTargets `hamburgerOverlay` element.\\nFor example:\\n\\n```css\\n.hamburger-overlay {\\n  background-color: #116dff;\\n}\\n```\\n\",\"displayName\":\"CSS Classes\",\"slugifyName\":\"css-classes\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is displayed on all pages\",\"content\":\"let isGlobal = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").global; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // \\\"page1\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").type; // \\\"$w.Type\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"children\",\"slug\":\"children\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's children\",\"content\":\"let myChildren = $w(\\\"#myContainer\\\").children;\\n\\nlet firstChild = myChildren[0];\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\"}},\"description\":\"Gets an array of the elements that are contained within the element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements, such as pages, headers, footers, and boxes, can contain\\r\\n other elements. This occurs when you drag an element onto a container\\r\\n element and [attach it](https://www.wix.com/support/html5/article/attaching-elements-to-a-box).\\r\\n These attached elements are considered the parent element's children.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Header\",\"slug\":\"header\",\"fqn\":\"Header\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse enters an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseIn( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved onto the\\r\\n element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n onto the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseOut\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseOut\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-out\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse exits an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseOut( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved off of\\r\\n the element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n off of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportEnter\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportEnter\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-enter\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has entered the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportEnter( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has left the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportLeave( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Node.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo();\"},{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo()\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with scroll\\\");\\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onClick\",\"slug\":\"on-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Change the background color of the element that was clicked\",\"content\":\"$w('#myElement').onClick((event) =\u003e {\\n  const clickedElement = event.target;\\n  clickedElement.style.backgroundColor = 'blue';\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `click` event when a user clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** To avoid unpredictable behavior, don't set redirect links in the editor for elements that already have an `onClick` event handler.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onDblClick\",\"fqn\":\"ClickableMixin.onDblClick\",\"slug\":\"on-dbl-click\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that was double-clicked\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onDblClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element is clicked.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the element is double-clicked.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element receives a `dblClick` event when a user double-clicks on the element\\r\\n and releases.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a user double-clicks an element, two `click` events are fired\\r\\n before a `doubleClick` event is also fired.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nThe header is located at the top of the page:\\n\\n ![Wix Page Header](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_header.png \\\"Wix Page Header\\\")\\n\\n The header is a container that can contain other elements.\\n\\n The contained elements are the header's [children](#children) and the\\n header is the contained elements' [parent](#parent).\\n\\n The same header appears on all pages of your site. Therefore, The children\\n elements of a header appear on all pages of your site.\\n\\n The `Header` is part of the [`Document`]($w.Document.html).\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"},{\"content\":\"\u003c!-- This article was published using the Doc Push single-sourcing tool. Any changes to this article MUST be made in the source file. Find it at www.github.com/wix-private/velo-docs.--\u003e\\n\\n# Header CSS Classes\\n\\n\u003e **Note:** This feature is only available to Wix Studio users.\\n\\nYou can use the classes listed below\\nto style your `Header` elements with CSS.\\n\\nFor more information on styling your elements with CSS, see\\n[Styling Elements with CSS]($w/styling-elements-with-css) and the\\n[MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\\n\\n\u003cblockquote class=\\\"important\\\"\u003e\\n\\n__Important:__\\nElement structure and undocumented class names\\nmay change without advance warning.\\nTo avoid unintended style changes to your site,\\nselect elements with the documented class names only.\\n\\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\\n\\n## `.header`\\n\\nTargets header elements.\\nFor example:\\n\\n```css\\n.header {\\n  margin-bottom: 25px;\\n  padding: 100px;\\n  border-bottom: 5px solid black;\\n}\\n```\\n\",\"displayName\":\"CSS Classes\",\"slugifyName\":\"css-classes\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"style\",\"slug\":\"style\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set the background color\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").style.backgroundColor = \\\"rgba(255,0,0,0.5)\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Get the background color\",\"content\":\"let bgColor = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").style.backgroundColor;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Style\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Style.Style\"},\"description\":\"Gets an object containing information about the header's styles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe following styles can be used with headers:\\r\\n\\r\\n + [`backgroundColor`]($w.Style.html#backgroundColor)\\r\\n + [`borderColor`]($w.Style.html#borderColor)\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is displayed on all pages\",\"content\":\"let isGlobal = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").global; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // \\\"page1\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").type; // \\\"$w.Type\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"children\",\"slug\":\"children\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's children\",\"content\":\"let myChildren = $w(\\\"#myContainer\\\").children;\\n\\nlet firstChild = myChildren[0];\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\"}},\"description\":\"Gets an array of the elements that are contained within the element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements, such as pages, headers, footers, and boxes, can contain\\r\\n other elements. This occurs when you drag an element onto a container\\r\\n element and [attach it](https://www.wix.com/support/html5/article/attaching-elements-to-a-box).\\r\\n These attached elements are considered the parent element's children.\"}]},{\"name\":\"HiddenCollapsedElement\",\"slug\":\"hidden-collapsed-element\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedElement\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[]},{\"name\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin\",\"slug\":\"hidden-collapsed-mixin\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[]},{\"name\":\"HiddenMixin\",\"slug\":\"hidden-mixin\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenMixin\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[]},{\"name\":\"Hover\",\"slug\":\"hover\",\"fqn\":\"Hover\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[]},{\"name\":\"HtmlComponent\",\"slug\":\"html-component\",\"fqn\":\"HtmlComponent\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"allowFullScreen\",\"fqn\":\"HtmlComponent.allowFullScreen\",\"slug\":\"allow-full-screen\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"HtmlComponent\",\"referenceFqn\":\"HtmlComponent.HtmlComponent\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Allow an HTML Component to be placed in full screen mode\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").allowFullScreen();\"}],\"description\":\"Allows the HTML Component to be put into full screen mode.\\r\\n\\r\\nBy default, users cannot place the HTML Component in full screen mode. Calling\\r\\n this function allows a user to place the HTML Component in full screen mode.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMessage\",\"fqn\":\"HtmlComponent.onMessage\",\"slug\":\"on-message\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"HtmlComponent\",\"referenceFqn\":\"HtmlComponent.HtmlComponent\",\"description\":\"The HTML Code element that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Receive a message from an HTML Component\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").onMessage( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let receivedMessage = event.data;\\n} );\"},{\"title\":\"Communicate with an HTML Component\",\"description\":\"This example shows how to send information from the page to the HTML Component and from the HTML Component to the page. \\n You can test out the code in our [example template](https://manage.wix.com/edit-template/from?originTemplateId=d39789d7-13ee-4208-8467-8a939cd8ed8c\u0026templateId=cfd24f07-e15f-4091-b110-2b8b889fa1e3\u0026autoDevMode=true).\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady(() =\u003e {\\n  // Send message to HTML Component\\n  $w('#sendButton').onClick(() =\u003e {\\n    $w('#htmlComponent').postMessage('HELLO FROM THE PAGE');\\n  });\\n\\n  // Handle messages that the HTML Component sends to the page\\n  $w('#htmlComponent').onMessage((event) =\u003e {\\n    $w('#message').text = event.data;\\n  });\\n});\"},{\"title\":\"Send a message to an HTML Component and receive a confirmation\",\"description\":\"This example assumes you have created a page with an HTML Component\\n whose ID is `myHtmlComponent` and a button whose onClick event handler\\n is set to `messageSendButton_onClick`.\\n\\n When the user clicks the button, a message is sent to the HTML Code\\n element. Code inside the element receives and displays the message. Then\\n it sends a message back to the page code. The page code receives and\\n logs the message.\",\"content\":\"/* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *\\n * Paste the following into the HTML Component:  *\\n * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *\\n\\n\u003c!doctype html\u003e\\n\u003chtml\u003e\\n\u003chead\u003e\\n\\n\u003cscript type=\\\"text/javascript\\\"\u003e\\nfunction init () {\\n  // when a message is received from the page code\\n  window.onmessage = (event) =\u003e {\\n    if (event.data) {\\n      console.log(\\\"HTML Code Element received a message!\\\");\\n      insertMessage(event.data);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// display received message\\nfunction insertMessage(msg) {\\n  document.getElementById('demo').innerHTML = msg;\\n  sendReturnMessage(\\\"Message from the HTML Component!\\\");\\n}\\n\\n// send message to the page code\\nfunction sendReturnMessage(msg) {\\n  window.parent.postMessage(msg, \\\"http://mysite.com\\\");\\n}\\n\u003c/script\u003e\\n\\n\u003c/head\u003e\\n\\n\u003cbody onload=\\\"init();\\\" style=\\\"background-color:lightgray;\\\"\u003e\\n\u003ch1\u003eHTML Component Test\u003c/h1\u003e\\n\u003cp id=\\\"demo\\\"\u003eMessage will go here\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/body\u003e\\n\u003c/html\u003e\\n\\n * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *\\n * This is the page code:                        *\\n * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * */\\n\\n$w.onReady(function () {\\n  // when a message is received from the HTML Component\\n  $w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").onMessage( (event) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(`Message received by page code: ${event.data}`);\\n  } );\\n} );\\n\\nexport function messageSendButton_onClick() {\\n  // send message to the HTML Component\\n  $w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").postMessage(\\\"Message from page code!\\\");\\n}\\n\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"HtmlComponentMessageEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"HtmlComponentMessageEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the HTML Component sends a message.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the HTML Component\\r\\n sends a message.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `onMessage()` function allows your page code to receive messages\\r\\n from an HTML Component on your page. When a message is received,\\r\\n the specified event handler is executed and the message can be retrieved\\r\\n using `event.data`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To send a message from your HTML Component, use the postMessage() function\\r\\n in the HTML component's code. Generally, you call postMessage()\\r\\n from within a function:\\r\\n\\r\\n     \\r\\n       function sendReturnMessage(msg) {\\r\\n         window.parent.postMessage(msg, \\\"http://mysite.com\\\");\\r\\n       }\\r\\n     \\r\\n\\r\\n When posting a message from within your HTML Component, you should specify your\\r\\n site's URL as the `targetOrigin`. If you use `\\\"*\\\"` instead, your message can\\r\\n be intercepted by a malicious site. To learn more, see [Window.postMessage()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/postMessage).\\r\\n\\r\\n For more information on sending and receiving messages between your page\\r\\n and your HTML Component, see [Working with the HTML Component in Wix Code](https://support.wix.com/en/article/working-with-the-html-component-in-wix-code#messaging-1).\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"postMessage\",\"fqn\":\"HtmlComponent.postMessage\",\"slug\":\"post-message\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"message\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Send a message to an HTML Component\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").postMessage(\\\"Message from page code!\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Communicate with an HTML Component\",\"description\":\"This example shows how to send information from the page to the HTML Component and from the HTML Component to the page. \\n You can test out the code in our [example template](https://manage.wix.com/edit-template/from?originTemplateId=d39789d7-13ee-4208-8467-8a939cd8ed8c\u0026templateId=cfd24f07-e15f-4091-b110-2b8b889fa1e3\u0026autoDevMode=true).\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady(() =\u003e {\\n  // Send message to HTML Component\\n  $w('#sendButton').onClick(() =\u003e {\\n    $w('#htmlComponent').postMessage('HELLO FROM THE PAGE');\\n  });\\n\\n  // Handle messages that the HTML Component sends to the page\\n  $w('#htmlComponent').onMessage((event) =\u003e {\\n    $w('#message').text = event.data;\\n  });\\n});\"},{\"title\":\"Send a message to an HTML Component and receive a confirmation\",\"description\":\"This example assumes you have created a page with an HTML Component\\n whose ID is `myHtmlComponent` and a button whose onClick event handler\\n is set to `messageSendButton_onClick`.\\n\\n When the user clicks the button, a message is sent to the HTML Code\\n element. Code inside the element receives and displays the message. Then\\n it sends a message back to the page code. The page code receives and\\n logs the message.\",\"content\":\"/* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *\\n * Paste the following into the HTML Component:  *\\n * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *\\n\\n\u003c!doctype html\u003e\\n\u003chtml\u003e\\n\u003chead\u003e\\n\\n\u003cscript type=\\\"text/javascript\\\"\u003e\\nfunction init () {\\n  // when a message is received from the page code\\n  window.onmessage = (event) =\u003e {\\n    if (event.data) {\\n      console.log(\\\"HTML Code Element received a message!\\\");\\n      insertMessage(event.data);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// display received message\\nfunction insertMessage(msg) {\\n  document.getElementById('demo').innerHTML = msg;\\n  sendReturnMessage(\\\"Message from the HTML Component!\\\");\\n}\\n\\n// send message to the page code\\nfunction sendReturnMessage(msg) {\\n  window.parent.postMessage(msg, \\\"http://mysite.com\\\");\\n}\\n\u003c/script\u003e\\n\\n\u003c/head\u003e\\n\\n\u003cbody onload=\\\"init();\\\" style=\\\"background-color:lightgray;\\\"\u003e\\n\u003ch1\u003eHTML Component Test\u003c/h1\u003e\\n\u003cp id=\\\"demo\\\"\u003eMessage will go here\u003c/p\u003e\\n\u003c/body\u003e\\n\u003c/html\u003e\\n\\n * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *\\n * This is the page code:                        *\\n * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * */\\n\\n$w.onReady(function () {\\n  // when a message is received from the HTML Component\\n  $w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").onMessage( (event) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(`Message received by page code: ${event.data}`);\\n  } );\\n} );\\n\\nexport function messageSendButton_onClick() {\\n  // send message to the HTML Component\\n  $w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").postMessage(\\\"Message from page code!\\\");\\n}\\n\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"message\",\"slug\":\"message\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"object\"},{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"any\"}}]},\"description\":\"The message to send to the HTML Component.\"}],\"description\":\"Sends a message to the HTML Component.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `postMessage()` function sends a message from your page code to the\\r\\n HTML Component.\\r\\n\\r\\n To receive the message sent from the `postMessage()` function in your\\r\\n HTML Component, create an event handler for the `window.onmessage` event\\r\\n in the component's code. You create the event handler within an HTML\\r\\n `` tag. You get the received data by getting the data property\\r\\n of the event handler's event parameter.\\r\\n\\r\\n Often, you define the `window.onMessage` event handler in a function\\r\\n that gets called when the HTML component loads using the `body onload`\\r\\n or `window.onload`:\\r\\n\\r\\n     \\r\\n       window.onmessage = (event) =\u003e {\\r\\n         if (event.data) {\\r\\n           console.log(`HTML Component received a message: ${event.data}`);\\r\\n           // additional code here\\r\\n         }\\r\\n       }\\r\\n     \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n For more information on sending and receiving messages between your page\\r\\n and your HTML Component, see [Working with the HTML Component in Wix Code](https://support.wix.com/en/article/working-with-the-html-component-in-wix-code#messaging-1).\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e + An HTML Component needs to load before you can send it messages using the `postMessage()` function.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + Usually an HTML Component finishes loading a\\r\\n\u003e   short time after the page it is on finishes loading. So if you call\\r\\n\u003e   `postMessage()` inside the page’s [`onReady()`]($w.html#onReady)\\r\\n\u003e   event handler, the HTML Component might not be ready yet.  To call `postMessage()`\\r\\n\u003e   as soon as possible after a page loads, send a\\r\\n\u003e   message from the HTML Component to the page code as when the HTML\\r\\n\u003e   Component is loaded and then call `postMessage()` upon receipt of that\\r\\n\u003e   message.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + Also, an HTML Component can send messages to the page it is on before the HTML Component\\r\\n\u003e   itself has loaded completely. For example, this can happen if the HTML Component’s body,\\r\\n\u003e   or one of its downloaded images, is large. To make sure the HTML component is loaded,\\r\\n\u003e   send messages only after listening for an onLoad event in the HTML component.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"collapse\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.collapse\",\"slug\":\"collapse\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"description\":\"Collapses the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `collapse()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a collapsed element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also collapse an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `collapse()` function doesn't remove elements from the DOM. \\r\\n \u003e To soft delete an element from the DOM, use the `delete()` function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"expand\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.expand\",\"slug\":\"expand\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"description\":\"Expands the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `expand()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an expanded element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, an element will not become visible by using `expand()` if it has been marked as \\\"Don't Display\\\" for the current breakpoint. Calling `expand()` will however, change the `collapsed` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e \\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `expand()` and `collapse()` with [**Hide**](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"hide\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.hide\",\"slug\":\"hide\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when hiding the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Hides the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `true`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `hide()` function hides the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `hide()` function doesn't remove the element from the DOM.\\r\\n \u003e To temporarily delete an element from the DOM and prevent it from detection by SEO crawlers, \\r\\n use the `delete()` function.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a hidden element,\\r\\n see the `hidden` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when hiding the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n Effects:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"arc\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"bounce\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fade\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"flip\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"float\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fly\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fold\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"glide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"puff\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"roll\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"slide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"spin\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"turn\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"zoom\\\"`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also hide an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse enters an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseIn( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved onto the\\r\\n element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n onto the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseOut\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseOut\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-out\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mouse event info when the mouse exits an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onMouseOut( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved off of\\r\\n the element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n off of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportEnter\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onViewportEnter\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-enter\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Restore a deleted element to the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\"},{\"title\":\"Restore an element to the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Element.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To use `scrollTo()` with a header element, the [Header Scroll Setting](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-changing-the-header-scroll-settings) must be set to **Scrolls with site**. To scroll to the header with other settings, use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"show\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenCollapsedMixin.show\",\"slug\":\"show\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when showing the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when showing the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n This table shows possible `effectName` values\\r\\n and their corresponding names in the editor:\\r\\n\\r\\n | Effect Name Value    | Editor Animation Name |\\r\\n | -------------------- | -------------------------- |\\r\\n | `\\\"arc\\\"`              | Arc-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"bounce\\\"`           | Bounce-In                  |\\r\\n | `\\\"fade\\\"`             | Fade-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"flip\\\"`             | Flip-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"float\\\"`            | Float-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"fly\\\"`              | Fly-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"fold\\\"`             | Fold-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"glide\\\"`            | Glide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"puff\\\"`             | Puff-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"roll\\\"`             | Reveal                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"slide\\\"`            | Slide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"spin\\\"`             | Spin-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"turn\\\"`             | Turn-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"zoom\\\"`             | Expand-In                  |\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, the `show ()` function will not make an element visible for a given breakpoint\\r\\n\u003e   if the element has been set to \\\"**Hide** for that breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\\r\\n\u003e   Calling `show()` however, will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `show()` and `hide()` with **Hide** and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nMessages can be sent\\n from your page code to the code in an HTML component and from the HTML\\n component to your page code using the [`postMessage()`](#postMessage) and\\n [`onMessage()`](#onMessage) functions. To learn more about what code an HTML\\n component can hold, see [here](https://support.wix.com/en/article/using-iframes-to-display-visible-content-on-your-site).\\n\\n Get hands-on experience with the HTML Components on our [Hello HTML Component](https://www.wix.com/velo/example/hello-html-component) example page. \\n\\n\u003e **Note:** To embed a PDF in an `HtmlComponent` you must upgrade your site to a [Premium Plan](https://support.wix.com/en/article/upgrading-your-site-to-premium-3066683).\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"},{\"content\":\"# Messaging Between a Site Page and an HTML iFrame Element\\n\\nYou can use code to send and receive messages between your page and your [HTML iFrame element](https://dev.wix.com/docs/develop-websites/articles/wix-editor-elements/other-elements/html-i-frame-element/working-with-the-html-iframe-element). You can send and receive data as any valid JavaScript type.\\n\\n\\n## Sending a Message from Page Code to an HTML Element\\n\\nYou can send a message from your page to an HTML element using the HTML element's `postMessage()` function.\\n\\nFor example, if your page contains an HTML element with the ID **myHtmlElement**:\\n\\n```javascript\\n$w(\\\"#myHtmlElement\\\").postMessage(\\\"Message for HTML Comp\\\");\\n```\\n\\n## Receiving a Message from Page Code in an HTML Element\\n\\nYou can receive a message in your HTML element by creating an event handler for the `window.onmessage` event in the element's code. You create the event handler within an HTML `\u003cscript\u003e` tag. You get the received data by getting the `data` property of the event handler's `event` parameter.\\n\\nFor example, in your HTML element's HTML Code:\\n\\n```html\\n\u003cscript type=\\\"text/javascript\\\"\u003e\\n  window.onmessage = (event) =\u003e {\\n    if (event.data) {\\n       let receivedData = event.data;\\n    }\\n  };\\n  \\n  //...\\n  \\n\u003c/script\u003e\\n```\\n\\n## Sending a Message from an HTML Element to Page Code\\n\\nYou can send a message from your HTML element using the `postMessage()` function in the element's code. Generally, you will be calling `postMessage()` from within a function.\\n\\nFor example, in your HTML element's HTML Code:\\n\\n```html\\n\u003cscript type=\\\"text/javascript\\\"\u003e\\n  \\n  //...\\n  \\n  function respond() {\\n    window.parent.postMessage(\\\"To page code\\\", \\\"http://mysite.com\\\");\\n  }\\n\u003c/script\u003e\\n```\\n\\n\u003cblockquote class=\\\"important\\\"\u003e\\n\\n**Important:** \\nWhen posting a message from within your HTML Component, you should specify your site's URL as the **targetOrigin**. If you use **\\\"\\\\*\\\"** instead, your message can be intercepted by a malicious site. To learn more, see [Window.postMessage()](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/postMessage).\\n\\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\\n\\n## Receiving a Message from an HTML Element in Page Code\\n\\nYou can receive a message in your page code using the HTML element's `onMessage()` function to bind an event handler. You get the received data by getting the `data` property of the event handler's `event` parameter.\\n\\nFor example, if your page contains an HTML element with the ID **myHtmlElement**:\\n\\n```javascript\\n$w(\\\"#myHtmlElement\\\").onMessage( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let receivedData = event.data;\\n} );\\n```\\n\",\"displayName\":\"Messaging Between a Site Page and an HTML Element\",\"slugifyName\":\"messaging-between-a-site-page-and-an-html-element\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"scrolling\",\"slug\":\"scrolling\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set whether the Html Component displays scrollbars\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").scrolling = \\\"no\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Get whether the Html Component displays scrollbars\",\"content\":\"let compScrolling = $w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").scrolling; // \\\"auto\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets whether the HTML Component displays scrollbars.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `scrolling` property sets what happens when the content in\\r\\n the HTML Component is larger than the size of the component.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value can be set to:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"auto\\\"`: Scrollbars are displayed only if needed. (This is the default.)\\r\\n + `\\\"yes\\\"`: Scrollbars are always shown, even if they are not needed.\\r\\n + `\\\"no\\\"`: Scrollbars are never shown, even if they are needed).\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the `scrolling` property returns which `ScrollType` the component\\r\\n is set to use.\"},{\"name\":\"src\",\"slug\":\"src\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the displayed website's URL\",\"content\":\"let compUrl = $w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").src;\\n// \\\"https://comp.com/page.html\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the displayed website\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").src = \\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTPS\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the URL of the HTML Component's code.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `src` property sets the website that is\\r\\n displayed in the HTML Component. The `src` value must be set to an HTTPS\\r\\n URL.\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the `src` property returns the URL of the website\\r\\n that is displayed in the HTML Component.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** The `src` property must be an HTTPS URL. Learn how to \\r\\n[embed a site with an HTTP URL](https://support.wix.com/en/article/velo-working-with-the-html-iframe-element#embedding-another-site).\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"}]},{\"name\":\"HtmlComponentMessageEvent\",\"slug\":\"html-component-message-event\",\"fqn\":\"HtmlComponentMessageEvent\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nEvent that is fired when the code in an HtmlComponent sends a message.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"data\",\"slug\":\"data\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Receive a message from an HTML Component\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myHtmlComponent\\\").onMessage( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let receivedMessage = event.data;\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"any\"},\"description\":\"Gets the event data.\"},{\"name\":\"context\",\"slug\":\"context\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the context of the event\",\"content\":\"// non-repeater event\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let type = event.context.type; // \\\"GLOBAL_SCOPE\\\"\\n} );\\n\\n\\n// repeater event\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myRepeatedElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let $item = $w.at(event.context)\\n  $item(\\\"#anotherRepeatedElement\\\").value = \\\"new value\\\";\\n\\n  let itemId = event.context.itemId;  // \\\"item1\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventContext\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Event.EventContext\"},\"description\":\"Gets the context in which an event was fired.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn event's `context` contains information about the circumstances\\r\\n surrounding the firing of the event.\\r\\n The context property only appears in events on repeated elements.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can use the event context with [`$w.at()`]($w.html#at) to get a\\r\\n selector function which selects items from a specific repeater item.\\r\\n It contains an object with one key:value pair. The key is \\\"itemId\\\" and\\r\\n the value is the ID of the repeated item on which the event occurred.\"},{\"name\":\"target\",\"slug\":\"target\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the target element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element that the event was fired on.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the type of the event\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let eventType = event.type; // \\\"click\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the type of event that was fired.\"}]},{\"name\":\"IFrame\",\"slug\":\"iframe\",\"fqn\":\"IFrame\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDepr