").restore()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with restore\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Restores a deleted element to the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `restore()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n See the [`delete`](#delete) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"scrollTo\",\"fqn\":\"Node.scrollTo\",\"slug\":\"scroll-to\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the scroll is complete.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo();\"},{\"title\":\"Scroll the page to an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").scrollTo()\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with scroll\\\");\\n} );\"}],\"description\":\"Scrolls the page to the top of the element using an animation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `scrollTo()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n animated scroll is complete and the element is in view.\\r\\n\\r\\n To scroll to a specific location on the page, see the `wix-window-frontend`\\r\\n [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function. \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Tip**: Use the `wix-window-frontend` [`scrollTo()`](wix-window-frontend.html#scrollTo) function to \\r\\n scroll directly to an element, and also disable the animation. \\r\\n To get the coordinates for scrolling, display the Wix Editor Toolbar. In the Editor, \\r\\n move the cursor to the top-left pixel where you want the page to scroll to. The **X** \\r\\n and **Y** axis **Position** values show the coordinates.\\r\\n \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** \\r\\n \u003e To