e element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mobile element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w('#myMobileElement').type; // '$w.Type'\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the mobile element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.MobileButton`\\r\\n - `$w.MobileSwitch`\\r\\n - `$w.MobilePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.MobileText`\\r\\n - `$w.MobileTextInput`\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the app under\\r\\n any circumstances. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the app. \\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the app loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the app under\\r\\n any circumstances. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the app as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden on load** in the Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the app loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden` and `collapsed` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the app. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `hidden` and \\r\\n `collapsed` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\"}]},{\"name\":\"MobileTextInput\",\"slug\":\"mobile-text-input\",\"fqn\":\"MobileTextInput\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"onChange\",\"fqn\":\"MobileValueMixin.onChange\",\"slug\":\"on-change\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MobileElement\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MobileElement.MobileElement\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the value of the element that was changed\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").onChange( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let newValue = event.target.value;  // \\\"new value\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element's value changes.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an input element's value\\r\\n is changed.\\r\\n\\r\\nA mobile element receives a `change` event when a mobile app user changes the value\\r\\n in an input element.\\r\\n\\r\\n A `change` event is not triggered when you change an element's value using\\r\\n the element's [`value`](#value) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n Because `onChange()` is fired before validations are performed, do not check \\r\\n any of the validation properties in the `onChange()` event handler. For example, \\r\\n do not code an `if` statement that checks the `valid` property in the `onChange()` event handler,\\r\\n because the property at this point contains values prior to validation.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"collapse\",\"fqn\":\"MobileHiddenCollapsedMixin.collapse\",\"slug\":\"collapse\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Collapse an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapse();\"},{\"title\":\"Collapse an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapse()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with collapse\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Collapses the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `collapse()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a collapsed element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also collapse an element\\r\\n when the app loads by using the Properties panel in the Editor.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"expand\",\"fqn\":\"MobileHiddenCollapsedMixin.expand\",\"slug\":\"expand\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Expand an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").expand();\"},{\"title\":\"Expand an element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").expand()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with expand\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Expands the element and sets its `collapsed` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `expand()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `collapsed` property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an expanded element,\\r\\n see the `collapsed` property.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"hide\",\"fqn\":\"MobileHiddenMixin.hide\",\"slug\":\"hide\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `hidden` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Hide an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hide();\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Hides the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `hide()` function hides the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a hidden element,\\r\\n see the `hidden` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also hide an element\\r\\n when the app loads by using the Properties panel in the Editor.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"show\",\"fqn\":\"MobileHiddenMixin.show\",\"slug\":\"show\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `hidden` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Show an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").show();\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** Calling `show()` will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"disable\",\"fqn\":\"MobileDisabledMixin.disable\",\"slug\":\"disable\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the mobile element's `enabled` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Disable a mobile element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").disable();\"},{\"title\":\"Disable a mobile element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").disable()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Element now disabled\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle a mobile element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Disables the mobile element and sets its `enabled` property to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `disable()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the mobile\\r\\n element's [`enabled`](#enabled) property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a disabled element,\\r\\n see the [`enabled`](#enabled) property.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"enable\",\"fqn\":\"MobileDisabledMixin.enable\",\"slug\":\"enable\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the mobile element's `enabled` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Enable an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enable();\"},{\"title\":\"Enable a mobile element and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enable()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Element now enabled\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle a mobile element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"description\":\"Enables the mobile element and sets its `enabled` property to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `enable()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the mobile\\r\\n element's [`enabled`](#enabled) property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of an enabled element,\\r\\n see the [`enabled`](#enabled) property.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\n\u003cblockquote class=\\\"important\\\"\u003e\\n\\n__Important:__\\n+ This API is only relevant for custom widgets in [Branded Apps](https://www.wix.com/app-builder).\\n+ Custom widgets are not yet available to all users. \\n+ This API is in [Developer Preview](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/api-overview/developer-preview) and is subject to change. \\n\\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\\n\\n\\nA text input is configured to receive\\n[different types of information](https://support.wix.com/en/article/input-settings), such as strings, numbers, or passwords.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"placeholder\",\"slug\":\"placeholder\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an input element's placeholder text\",\"content\":\"let myPlaceholder = $w('#mobileTextInput1').placeholder; // 'Enter your first name'\"},{\"title\":\"Set an input element's placeholder text\",\"content\":\"$w('#mobileTextInput1').placeholder = 'Enter your first name';\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the input element's placeholder text.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlaceholder text is typically used to provide a\\r\\n hint to the mobile app user of what to enter into an input element that accepts\\r\\n text. When the mobile app user begins to enter text, the placeholder text disappears.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mobile element's ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w('#myMobileElement').id; // 'myMobileElement'\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the mobile element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `id` property is the the mobile element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting mobile\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent mobile element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w('#myMobileElement').parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // 'container1'\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the mobile element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome mobile elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n a mobile element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the mobile element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w('#myMobileElement').type; // '$w.Type'\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the mobile element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.MobileButton`\\r\\n - `$w.MobileSwitch`\\r\\n - `$w.MobilePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.MobileText`\\r\\n - `$w.MobileTextInput`\"},{\"name\":\"label\",\"slug\":\"label\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's label\",\"content\":\"let label = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").label;  // \\\"Submit\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set an element's label\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").label = \\\"New Label\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the label of an element.\"},{\"name\":\"valid\",\"slug\":\"valid\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether the element is valid\",\"content\":\"let isValid = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").valid; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an input element's value is valid.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `valid` property indicates if an input element's value satisfies\\r\\n all conditions defined in the [`validations`](#validations) property to pass a validation check.\"},{\"name\":\"validateOnBlur\",\"slug\":\"validate-on-blur\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether to validate the mobile element on blur\",\"content\":\"let validateElementOnBlur = $w('#myMobileElement').validateOnBlur; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Set whether to validate the mobile element on blur\",\"content\":\"$w('#myMobileElement').validateOnBlur = true;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets whether to validate the mobile element when it loses focus.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element loses focus (blurs) through user actions, such as pressing a button or another input element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n If `validateOnBlur` is `true`, the mobile element will validate when it loses focus.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `validateOnBlur` is `false`, the mobile element won't validate when it loses focus.\"},{\"name\":\"validateOnChange\",\"slug\":\"validate-on-change\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether to validate the mobile element on change\",\"content\":\"let validateElementOnChange = $w('#myMobileElement').validateOnChange; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Set whether to validate the mobile element on change\",\"content\":\"$w('#myMobileElement').validateOnChange = true;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets whether to validate the mobile element when its value changes.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `validateOnChange` is `true`, the mobile element will validate when its value changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `validateOnChange` is `false`, the mobile element won't validate when its value changes.\"},{\"name\":\"validateOnStart\",\"slug\":\"validate-on-start\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether to validate the mobile element when it is loaded\",\"content\":\"let validateElementOnStart = $w('#myMobileElement').validateOnStart; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Set whether to validate the mobile element when it is loaded\",\"content\":\"$w('#myMobileElement').validateOnStart = true;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets whether to validate the mobile element when it is loaded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `validateOnStart` is `true`, the mobile element will validate when it is finished loading.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `validateOnStart` is `false`, the mobile element won't validate when it is finished loading.\"},{\"name\":\"validations\",\"slug\":\"validations\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set the mobile element's validations\",\"content\":\"$w('#mobileTextInput1').validations = [\\n  { validationType: 'required', message: 'This field is required.' },\\n  { validationType: 'url', message: 'Not a valid URL.' }\\n];\"},{\"title\":\"Get the mobile element's validations\",\"content\":\"let myMobileTextInputValidation = $w('#mobileTextInput1').validations; // [{ validationType: 'required', message: 'This field is required.' }, { validationType: 'url', message: 'Not a valid URL.' }]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"ARRAY\",\"elementType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Validation\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MobileValueMixin.Validation\"}},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the validations for mobile elements in a form.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `validations` property sets the validations for mobile elements in a form.\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the `validations` property returns the current list of validation objects for mobile elements in a form.\\r\\n\\r\\n Each validation object contains a `validationType` and a validation `message`.\"},{\"name\":\"value\",\"slug\":\"value\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mobile element's value\",\"content\":\"let myValue = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").value; // \\\"42\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set a mobile element's value\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").value = \\\"42\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"any\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets an element's value.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `value` property's type depends on the element implementing it. \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e + Changing an element's `value` in code does not trigger an `onChange` event.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + If an element is connected to a dataset, setting the element's `value`\\r\\n\u003e   in code does not set the value of the connected field in the dataset.\\r\\n\u003e   That means if you use the dataset to perform a submit, the value changed\\r\\n\u003e   in code is not reflected in the submitted item.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + To submit the new value using a dataset, set the field's value using the\\r\\n\u003e   [`setFieldValue()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/set-field-value) function before\\r\\n\u003e   performing the submit.\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the app under\\r\\n any circumstances. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the app. \\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the app loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the app under\\r\\n any circumstances. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the app as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden on load** in the Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the app loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the app.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden` and `collapsed` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the app. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `hidden` and \\r\\n `collapsed` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\"},{\"name\":\"enabled\",\"slug\":\"enabled\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mobile element's enabled status\",\"content\":\"let isEnabled = $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enabled; // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle a mobile element's enabled state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enabled ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").disable();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myMobileElement\\\").enable();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the mobile element is enabled or disabled.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `enabled` is `true`, users can interact with the mobile element.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `enabled` is `false`, users cannot interact with the mobile element.\\r\\n\\r\\n When an element is disabled:\\r\\n\\r\\n + Its color is faded or grayed out.\\r\\n + Actions that the element has been configured to perform, such as\\r\\n   opening a link, do not occur.\\r\\n + Event handlers that have been bound to the element, such as with\\r\\n   `onPressIn`, do not run.\\r\\n + If the element is an input element, such as a text box,\\r\\n   users cannot interact with it.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `enabled` property of a mobile element, use the element's\\r\\n [`enable()`](#enable) or [`disable()`](#disable) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n The `enabled` property can also be set in the Editor using the Properties and Events panel.\"}]},{\"name\":\"MobileValueMixin\",\"slug\":\"mobile-value-mixin\",\"fqn\":\"MobileValueMixin\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[]},{\"name\":\"MouseEvent\",\"slug\":\"mouse-event\",\"fqn\":\"MouseEvent\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nThe properties of a `MouseEvent` refer to the client, page, and screen.\\n These terms refer to different containers as shown in the diagrams below.\\n\\n ![Coordinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_client.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\\n\\n ![Coordinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_page.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\\n\\n ![Coordinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_screen.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"clientX\",\"slug\":\"client-x\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n left edge of the browser's viewable area.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe browser's viewable area refers to the viewable contents\\r\\n of the page and excludes elements such as a sidebar and scrollbar.\\r\\n Therefore, two clicks on the same physical point of the screen\\r\\n return the same `clientX` values even if the page is scrolled horizontally in\\r\\n the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the page return different `clientX` values if the\\r\\n page is scrolled horizontally in the meantime.\\r\\n\\r\\n ![Coodinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_client.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\"},{\"name\":\"clientY\",\"slug\":\"client-y\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n top edge of the browser's viewable area.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe browser's viewable area refers to the viewable contents\\r\\n of the page and excludes elements such as a toolbar and scrollbar.\\r\\n Therefore, two clicks on the same physical point of the screen\\r\\n return the same `clientY` values if the page is scrolled vertically in\\r\\n the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the page return different `clientY` values if the\\r\\n page is scrolled vertically in the meantime.\\r\\n\\r\\n ![Coodinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_client.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\"},{\"name\":\"offsetX\",\"slug\":\"offset-x\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n left edge of the element that triggered this event.\\r\\n\\r\\nScrolling the web page causes its elements to shift relative to the\\r\\n browser window. Therefore, two clicks on the same physical point of the\\r\\n screen return different `offsetX` values if the page is scrolled\\r\\n horizontally in the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the element return the same `offsetX` values even if the\\r\\n page is scrolled horizontally in the meantime.\"},{\"name\":\"offsetY\",\"slug\":\"offset-y\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n top edge of the element that triggered this event.\\r\\n\\r\\nScrolling the web page causes its elements to shift relative to the\\r\\n browser window. Therefore, two clicks on the same physical point of the\\r\\n screen return different `offsetY` values if the page is scrolled\\r\\n vertically in the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the element return the same `offsetY` values even if the\\r\\n page is scrolled horizontally in the meantime.\"},{\"name\":\"pageX\",\"slug\":\"page-x\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n left edge of the page.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe page refers to the entire web page, even parts that are\\r\\n not currently viewable in the browser. Therefore, two clicks on the same\\r\\n physical point of the screen return different `pageX` values if the\\r\\n page is scrolled horizontally in the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the page return the same `pageX` values even if the\\r\\n page is scrolled horizontally in the meantime.\\r\\n\\r\\n ![Coodinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_page.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\"},{\"name\":\"pageY\",\"slug\":\"page-y\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n top edge of the page.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe page refers to the entire web page, even parts that are\\r\\n not currently viewable in the browser. Therefore, two clicks on the same\\r\\n physical point of the screen return different `pageY` values if the\\r\\n page is scrolled vertically in the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the page return the same `pageY` values even if the\\r\\n page is scrolled vertically in the meantime.\\r\\n\\r\\n ![Coodinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_page.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\"},{\"name\":\"screenX\",\"slug\":\"screen-x\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n left edge of the screen or screens.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe screen refers to the physical screen or screens.\\r\\n Therefore, two clicks on the same physical point of the screen\\r\\n return the same `screenX` values even if the page is scrolled horizontally in\\r\\n the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the page return different `screenX` values if the\\r\\n page is scrolled horizontally in the meantime.\\r\\n\\r\\n ![Coodinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_screen.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\"},{\"name\":\"screenY\",\"slug\":\"screen-y\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a mouse click's coordinates\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onClick( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let clientX = event.clientX;  // 362\\n  let clientY = event.clientY;  // 244\\n  let offsetX = event.offsetX;  // 10\\n  let offsetY = event.offsetY;  // 12\\n  let pageX = event.pageX;      // 362\\n  let pageY = event.pageY;      // 376\\n  let screenX = event.screenX;  // 3897\\n  let screenY = event.screenY;  // 362\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the distance in pixels between the pointer and the\\r\\n top edge of the screen or screens.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe screen refers to the physical screen or screens.\\r\\n Therefore, two clicks on the same physical point of the screen\\r\\n return the same `screenY` values if the page is scrolled vertically in\\r\\n the meantime. But two clicks on the\\r\\n same point on the page return different `screenY` values if the\\r\\n page is scrolled vertically in the meantime.\\r\\n\\r\\n ![Coodinate Reference](https://wixmp-833713b177cebf373f611808.wixmp.com/images/velo-images/media_coordinates_screen.png \\\"Coordinate Reference\\\")\"},{\"name\":\"context\",\"slug\":\"context\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the context of the event\",\"content\":\"// non-repeater event\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let type = event.context.type; // \\\"GLOBAL_SCOPE\\\"\\n} );\\n\\n\\n// repeater event\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myRepeatedElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let $item = $w.at(event.context)\\n  $item(\\\"#anotherRepeatedElement\\\").value = \\\"new value\\\";\\n\\n  let itemId = event.context.itemId;  // \\\"item1\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventContext\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Event.EventContext\"},\"description\":\"Gets the context in which an event was fired.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn event's `context` contains information about the circumstances\\r\\n surrounding the firing of the event.\\r\\n The context property only appears in events on repeated elements.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can use the event context with [`$w.at()`]($w.html#at) to get a\\r\\n selector function which selects items from a specific repeater item.\\r\\n It contains an object with one key:value pair. The key is \\\"itemId\\\" and\\r\\n the value is the ID of the repeated item on which the event occurred.\"},{\"name\":\"target\",\"slug\":\"target\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the target element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id;  // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element that the event was fired on.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the type of the event\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onEvent( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let eventType = event.type; // \\\"click\\\"\\n} );\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the type of event that was fired.\"}]},{\"name\":\"MultiStateBox\",\"slug\":\"multi-state-box\",\"fqn\":\"MultiStateBox\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"changeState\",\"fqn\":\"MultiStateBox.changeState\",\"slug\":\"change-state\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"stateReference\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"State\",\"referenceFqn\":\"State.State\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - The state that the multi-state box changed to.\\r\\nRejected - Error message: If no argument was provided or the argument is not a string or an existing state.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Move to a new state using an id\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myStatebox\\\").changeState(\\\"state2\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Move to a new state using a [`State`]($w.State.html) object\",\"description\":\"This example moves to the state that is stored in the `state` variable.\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myStatebox\\\").changeState(state);\\n\"},{\"title\":\"Move to a new state and log a message when the move is finished\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myStatebox\\\").changeState(\\\"state2\\\")\\n  .then( (newState) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(`Done moving to ${newState.id}`);\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Switch between 2 states\",\"description\":\"This example demonstrates how to switch back and forth between 2 states. The multi-state box has 2 states, with IDs `state1` and `state2`. Each state has a button. When a site visitor clicks the button, the multi-state box moves to the other state.\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#buttonState1\\\").onClick(() =\u003e {\\n  $w('#myStatebox').changeState(\\\"state2\\\");\\n} );\\n\\n$w(\\\"#buttonState2\\\").onClick(() =\u003e {\\n  $w('#myStatebox').changeState(\\\"state1\\\");\\n} );\\n\"},{\"title\":\"Switch between 3 states\",\"description\":\"This example shows how to change between states in multi-state boxes using code. \\n You can test out the code in our [example template](https://manage.wix.com/edit-template/from?originTemplateId=65aa0783-be71-42bc-ac6b-c21b454748f5\u0026templateId=d87fbeb3-300c-49da-b93a-a2a5b4e620c6\u0026autoDevMode=true).\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady(() =\u003e {\\n  $w('#newYorkButton').onClick(() =\u003e {\\n    $w('#statebox').changeState('newYork');\\n  });\\n\\n  $w('#texasButton').onClick(() =\u003e {\\n    $w('#statebox').changeState('texas');\\n  });\\n\\n  $w('#californiaButton').onClick(() =\u003e {\\n    $w('#statebox').changeState('california');\\n  });\\n});\\n\"},{\"title\":\"State per Status\",\"description\":\"This example demonstrates how to display different product badges for products on a Wix Stores product page. When a site visitor navigates to a product, we check the product's status (out of stock, on sale) and change the state to display the appropriate badge.\",\"content\":\"wixLocationFrontend.onChange(() =\u003e {\\n  // Get all info on the current product\\n  $w('#myProductPage').getProduct()\\n    .then( (product) =\u003e {\\n      if (!product.inStock) {\\n        $w('#badgeStatebox').changeState(\\\"outOfStock\\\");\\n      }\\n      // If the price is different than the discount price, indicating a sale\\n      else if (product.price !== product.discountedPrice) {\\n        $w('#badgeStatebox').changeState(\\\"onSale\\\");\\n      }\\n      else {\\n        $w('#badgeStatebox').changeState(\\\"checkMeOut\\\");\\n      }\\n    } )\\n    .catch( (error) =\u003e {\\n      console.log(error);\\n    } );\\n} );\\n\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"stateReference\",\"slug\":\"state-reference\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"State\",\"referenceFqn\":\"State.State\"}]},\"description\":\"The state to move to. Either the [`id`]($w.State.html#id) of the state or a [`State`]($w.State.html) object from the multi-state box.\"}],\"description\":\"Change the multi-state box's current state to a specific state.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `changeState()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when\\r\\n the multi-state box finishes moving from the current state to the state\\r\\n referred to by `stateReference`. `stateReference` can be a state object or\\r\\n a state [`id`]($w.State.html#id).\\r\\n\\r\\n You can retrieve [`State`]($w.State.html) objects to pass to the\\r\\n `stateReference` parameter from your multi-state box using the\\r\\n [`currentState`](#currentState) or [`states`](#states) properties.\\r\\n \\r\\n \u003e **Note:**  \\r\\n \u003e If you call `changeState()` on a child multi-state box, it doesn't run until the parent box moves to the state where the child box is displayed.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onChange\",\"fqn\":\"MultiStateBox.onChange\",\"slug\":\"on-change\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"eventHandler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MultiStateBox\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MultiStateBox.MultiStateBox\",\"description\":\"The multi-state box on which the event