hat are contained within the element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements, such as pages, headers, footers, and boxes, can contain\\r\\n other elements. This occurs when you drag an element onto a container\\r\\n element and [attach it](https://www.wix.com/support/html5/article/attaching-elements-to-a-box).\\r\\n These attached elements are considered the parent element's children.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Pagination\",\"slug\":\"pagination\",\"fqn\":\"Pagination\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"onChange\",\"fqn\":\"Pagination.onChange\",\"slug\":\"on-change\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Pagination\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Pagination.Pagination\",\"description\":\"The pagination bar on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the new current page of the pagination bar that was changed\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myPagination\\\").onChange( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let newValue = event.target.currentPage;  // 4\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the item is ready.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the pagination bar\\r\\n is changed.\\r\\n\\r\\nA pagination bar receives a `change` event when a user changes the\\r\\n current page by interacting with the pagination bar.\\r\\n\\r\\n A `change` event is not triggered when you change a pagination bar's\\r\\n current page using the [`currentPage`](#currentPage) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n When a pagination bar is connected to a dataset, changing the [dataset's\\r\\n current page](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/introduction#dataset-pages) using dataset functions, such\\r\\n as [`nextPage()`](https://dev.wix.com/docs/velo/api-reference/$w/dataset/next-page), do not trigger `change`\\r\\n events on the pagination bar.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\