oldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when showing the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n This table shows possible `effectName` values\\r\\n and their corresponding names in the editor:\\r\\n\\r\\n | Effect Name Value    | Editor Animation Name |\\r\\n | -------------------- | -------------------------- |\\r\\n | `\\\"arc\\\"`              | Arc-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"bounce\\\"`           | Bounce-In                  |\\r\\n | `\\\"fade\\\"`             | Fade-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"flip\\\"`             | Flip-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"float\\\"`            | Float-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"fly\\\"`              | Fly-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"fold\\\"`             | Fold-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"glide\\\"`            | Glide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"puff\\\"`             | Puff-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"roll\\\"`             | Reveal                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"slide\\\"`            | Slide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"spin\\\"`             | Spin-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"turn\\\"`             | Turn-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"zoom\\\"`             | Expand-In                  |\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, the `show ()` function will not make an element visible for a given breakpoint\\r\\n\u003e   if the element has been set to \\\"**Hide** for that breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\\r\\n\u003e   Calling `show()` however, will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `show()` and `hide()` with **Hide** and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nAn element that displays a video.\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"videoUrl\",\"slug\":\"video-url\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set the video to play\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideo\\\").videoUrl = \\\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=PMWmYf2043g\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Get the video to play\",\"content\":\"let videoUrl = $w(\\\"#myVideo\\\").videoUrl;\\n// \\\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=PMWmYf2043g\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the URL of the video.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Deprecation Note:** This video player has been deprecated. Use the\\r\\n [VideoPlayer]($w.VideoPlayer.html) element instead.\\r\\n\\r\\n Setting the value of the `videoUrl` property sets the video that the\\r\\n element plays.\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the value of the `videoUrl` property gets the URL of the video\\r\\n that the element plays.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is displayed on all pages\",\"content\":\"let isGlobal = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").global; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // \\\"page1\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").type; // \\\"$w.Type\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"}]},{\"name\":\"VideoBox\",\"slug\":\"video-box\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"mute\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.mute\",\"slug\":\"mute\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the volume has been muted.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Mute volume\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").mute();\"},{\"title\":\"Mute volume and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").mute()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with mute\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Mutes video box volume.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onEnded\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.onEnded\",\"slug\":\"on-ended\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"VideoBox\",\"referenceFqn\":\"VideoBox.VideoBox\",\"description\":\"The video box that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the video box whose video has ended\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").onEnded( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myVideoBox\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the video has ended.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the playback has ended.\\r\\n\\r\\nA video ends when the playback reaches the [`duration`](#duration) of the video.\\r\\n\\r\\n If the video is set to play in a loop, this event handler is never triggered.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved onto the\\r\\n element.\"}],\"description\":\"**Note: This standard element property is not relevant for VideoBox.**\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n onto the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseOut\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.onMouseOut\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-out\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element to which the event handler was added.\"},\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"MouseEventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the pointer is moved off of\\r\\n the element.\"}],\"description\":\"**Note: This standard element property is not relevant for VideoBox.**\\r\\n\\r\\nAdds an event handler that runs when the pointer is moved\\r\\n off of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onPause\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.onPause\",\"slug\":\"on-pause\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"VideoBox\",\"referenceFqn\":\"VideoBox.VideoBox\",\"description\":\"The video box that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the video box that has been paused\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").onPause( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myVideoBox\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the video is paused.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the playback is paused.\\r\\n\\r\\nA video in a video box is paused when a site visitor clicks the video box's\\r\\n pause button or by calling its [`pause()`](#pause) or [`stop()`](#stop) functions.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onPlay\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.onPlay\",\"slug\":\"on-play\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"VideoBox\",\"referenceFqn\":\"VideoBox.VideoBox\",\"description\":\"The video box that triggered the event.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the video box that is playing\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").onPlay( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myVideoBox\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the video in the video box is played.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the playback is started or restarted.\\r\\n\\r\\nA video in a video box is played when a site visitor clicks the video box's\\r\\n play button or by calling its [`play()`](#play) function.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onProgress\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.onProgress\",\"slug\":\"on-progress\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"VideoBox\",\"referenceFqn\":\"VideoBox.VideoBox\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the video box that is progressing\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").onProgress( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myVideoBox\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the video progresses.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when the playback progresses.\\r\\n\\r\\nA video continually progresses as the video plays.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"pause\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.pause\",\"slug\":\"pause\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the playback has been paused.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Pause playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").pause();\"},{\"title\":\"Pause playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").pause()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with pause\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Pauses playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `pause()` function pauses the current video and fires a `pause` event.\\r\\n\\r\\n The [onPause( )](#onPause) event handler is called.\\r\\n\\r\\n Any event handlers [set in the Editor](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-about-videoboxes#change-the-behavior-of-your-videobox) are also called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"play\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.play\",\"slug\":\"play\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the playback begins or resumes.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Begin or resume playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").play();\"},{\"title\":\"Begin or resume playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").play()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with play\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Begins or resumes playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `play()` function plays the current video and fires a `play` event.\\r\\n\\r\\n The [onPlay( )](#onPlay) event handler is called.\\r\\n\\r\\n Any event handlers [set in the Editor](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-about-videoboxes#change-the-behavior-of-your-videobox) are also called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"stop\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.stop\",\"slug\":\"stop\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the playback has been stopped.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Stop playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").stop();\"},{\"title\":\"Stop playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").stop()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with stop\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Stops the playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `stop()` function stops the current playback,\\r\\n moves to the beginning of the video, and fires a `pause` event.\\r\\n\\r\\n The [onPause( )](#onPause) event handler is called.\\r\\n\\r\\n Any event handlers [set in the Editor](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-about-videoboxes#change-the-behavior-of-your-videobox) are also called.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"togglePlay\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.togglePlay\",\"slug\":\"toggle-play\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the playback has been toggled.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Toggle playback\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").togglePlay();\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle playback and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").togglePlay()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with toggle play\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Toggles playback.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `togglePlay()` function either pauses or plays the current video based\\r\\n on its current state:\\r\\n\\r\\n + If the video is paused, it plays and a `play` event is fired. The\\r\\n   `play` event handlers set on the video box by the [onPlay( )](#onPlay)\\r\\n   function are called. (Any event handlers [set in the Editor](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-about-videoboxes#change-the-behavior-of-your-videobox) are also called.)\\r\\n + If the video is playing, it is paused and a `pause` event is fired. The\\r\\n   `pause` event handlers set on the video box by the [onPause( )](#onPause)\\r\\n   function are called.  (Any event handlers [set in the Editor](https://support.wix.com/en/article/wix-editor-about-videoboxes#change-the-behavior-of-your-videobox) are also called.)\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"unmute\",\"fqn\":\"VideoBox.unmute\",\"slug\":\"unmute\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the volume has been unmuted.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Unmute volume\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").unmute();\"},{\"title\":\"Unmute volume and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoBox\\\").unmute()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with unmute\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Unmutes video volume.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportEnter\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportEnter\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-enter\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has entered the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportEnter( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element enters the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is displayed\\r\\n in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element enters the viewport when the page is scrolled to show any\\r\\n part of the element. An element also enters the viewport if it was\\r\\n `hidden` or `collapsed`\\r\\n and is then shown or expanded in the viewable part of the current window. `onViewportEnter()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled into view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onViewportLeave\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin.onViewportLeave\",\"slug\":\"on-viewport-leave\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"handler\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Element\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Element.Element\",\"description\":\"The element on which the event is now registered.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID of the element that has left the viewport\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewportLeave( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let targetId = event.target.id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"handler\",\"slug\":\"handler\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventHandler\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EventHandler\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The name of the function or\\r\\n the function expression to run when the element leaves the viewport.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when an element is no longer\\r\\n displayed in the viewable part of the current window.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn element leaves the viewport when the page is scrolled so that the\\r\\n element is completely out of view. An element also leaves the viewport\\r\\n if it was shown or expanded and is then `hidden`\\r\\n or `collapsed` from the viewable part\\r\\n of the current window.  `onViewportLeave()` \\r\\n is not fired for `hidden` or `collapsed` \\r\\n elements even if they are scrolled out of view.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"restore\",\"fqn\":\"Element.restore\",\"slug\":\"restore\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionError