":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Hides the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `true`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `hide()` function hides the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `true`.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e**Note:** The `hide()` function doesn't remove the element from the DOM.\\r\\n \u003e To temporarily delete an element from the DOM and prevent it from detection by SEO crawlers, \\r\\n use the `delete()` function.\\r\\n\\r\\n To learn about the behavior of a hidden element,\\r\\n see the `hidden` property.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when hiding the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n Effects:\\r\\n\\r\\n + `\\\"arc\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"bounce\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fade\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"flip\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"float\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fly\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"fold\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"glide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"puff\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"roll\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"slide\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"spin\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"turn\\\"`\\r\\n + `\\\"zoom\\\"`\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n You can also hide an element\\r\\n when the page loads by using the Properties and Events panel in the Editor.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"show\",\"fqn\":\"HiddenMixin.show\",\"slug\":\"show\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the effect is complete and the element's `hidden` property has been set to `false`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Show an element with no effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with the \\\"fade\\\" effect and custom options\",\"content\":\"let fadeOptions = {\\n  \\\"duration\\\":   2000,\\n  \\\"delay\\\":      1000\\n};\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\", fadeOptions);\"},{\"title\":\"Show an element with an effect and log a message when the effect is done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show(\\\"fade\\\")\\n  .then( ( ) =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with fade\\\");\\n  } );\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"effectName\",\"slug\":\"effect-name\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The name of the\\r\\n effect to play when showing the item.\"},{\"name\":\"effectOptions\",\"slug\":\"effect-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"UNION\",\"types\":[{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ArcEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ArcEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"BounceEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.BounceEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FadeEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FadeEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlipEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlipEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FloatEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FloatEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FlyEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FlyEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"FoldEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.FoldEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"GlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.GlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"PuffEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.PuffEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"RollEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.RollEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SlideEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SlideEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"SpinEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.SpinEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"TurnEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.TurnEffectOptions\"},{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ZoomEffectOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"EffectOptions.ZoomEffectOptions\"}]},\"description\":\"The effect's options.\"}],\"description\":\"Shows the element and sets its `hidden` property\\r\\n to `false`, using an effect if specified.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `show()` function shows the element and returns a Promise that is\\r\\n resolved when the effect is complete and the element's `hidden`\\r\\n property has been set to `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can optionally apply an effect when showing the element by providing\\r\\n an `effectName` value. You can also customize the effect by providing the\\r\\n optional `effectOptions` object.\\r\\n\\r\\n This table shows possible `effectName` values\\r\\n and their corresponding names in the editor:\\r\\n\\r\\n | Effect Name Value    | Editor Animation Name |\\r\\n | -------------------- | -------------------------- |\\r\\n | `\\\"arc\\\"`              | Arc-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"bounce\\\"`           | Bounce-In                  |\\r\\n | `\\\"fade\\\"`             | Fade-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"flip\\\"`             | Flip-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"float\\\"`            | Float-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"fly\\\"`              | Fly-In                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"fold\\\"`             | Fold-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"glide\\\"`            | Glide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"puff\\\"`             | Puff-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"roll\\\"`             | Reveal                     |\\r\\n | `\\\"slide\\\"`            | Slide-In                   |\\r\\n | `\\\"spin\\\"`             | Spin-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"turn\\\"`             | Turn-In                    |\\r\\n | `\\\"zoom\\\"`             | Expand-In                  |\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, the `show ()` function will not make an element visible for a given breakpoint\\r\\n\u003e   if the element has been set to \\\"**Hide** for that breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\\r\\n\u003e   Calling `show()` however, will change the `hidden` property of the element to `false`.\\r\\n\u003e + It is recommended **not** to mix `show()` and `hide()` with **Hide** and **Show** in Wix Studio.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]}],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[{\"content\":\"# Introduction\\nA video player allows you to present video from:\\n\\n + Dailymotion\\n + Facebook\\n + Twitch\\n + Vimeo\\n + YouTube\\n + Videos uploaded to your site\\n + Any online .mp4 file\",\"displayName\":\"Introduction\",\"slugifyName\":\"introduction\"},{\"content\":\"\u003c!-- This article was published using the Doc Push single-sourcing tool. Any changes to this article MUST be made in the source file. Find it at www.github.com/wix-private/velo-docs.--\u003e\\n\\n# VideoPlayer CSS Classes\\n\\n\u003e **Note:** This feature is only available to Wix Studio users.\\n\\nYou can use the classes listed below\\nto style your `VideoPlayer` elements with CSS.\\n\\nFor more information on styling your elements with CSS, see\\n[Styling Elements with CSS]($w/styling-elements-with-css) and the\\n[MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\\n\\n\u003cblockquote class=\\\"important\\\"\u003e\\n\\n__Important:__\\nElement structure and undocumented class names\\nmay change without advance warning.\\nTo avoid unintended style changes to your site,\\nselect elements with the documented class names only.\\n\\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\\n\\n## `.video-player`\\n\\nTargets VideoPlayer elements.\\nFor example:\\n\\n```css\\n.video-player {\\n  display: block;\\n  width: 1600px;\\n  height: 900px;\\n  filter: drop-shadow(16px 16px 10px gray);\\n}\\n```\\n\",\"displayName\":\"CSS Classes\",\"slugifyName\":\"css-classes\"}],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"currentTime\",\"slug\":\"current-time\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the current play time\",\"content\":\"let currentTime = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").currentTime // 137\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the current play time from the beginning of the current video, in seconds.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo set the `currentTime` property, use the [`seek()`](#seek) function.\"},{\"name\":\"description\",\"slug\":\"description\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a video player's description\",\"content\":\"let desc = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").description // \\\"Video description\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set a video player's description\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").description = \\\"Video description\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the description of a video.\\r\\n \u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n \u003e - Setting a video description only works when a video player is presenting a\\r\\n \u003e   video uploaded to your site.\\r\\n \u003e - Getting a video description does not work when a video player is presenting a\\r\\n \u003e   video from Facebook, Twitch, or YouTube.\"},{\"name\":\"duration\",\"slug\":\"duration\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the current video's duration\",\"content\":\"let duration = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").duration // 198\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Gets the total play time of the current video, in seconds.\"},{\"name\":\"isMuted\",\"slug\":\"is-muted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether the volume is muted\",\"content\":\"let isMuted = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").isMuted // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the volume is currently muted.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo set the `isMuted` property, use the [`mute()`](#mute)\\r\\n and [`unmute()`](#unmute) functions.\"},{\"name\":\"isPlaying\",\"slug\":\"is-playing\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether a video is playing\",\"content\":\"let isPlaying = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").isPlaying // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if a video is currently playing.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo set the `isPlaying` property, use the [`play()`](#play),\\r\\n [`pause()`](#pause), and [`stop()`](#stop) functions.\"},{\"name\":\"poster\",\"slug\":\"poster\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the current video's poster\",\"content\":\"let videoPoster = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").poster;\\n// \\\"wix:image://v1/11062b_7124ff06fc5649f5f4846ff000.jpg/_.jpg#originWidth=1920\u0026originHeight=1080\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the current video's poster to an image from the Media Manager\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").poster = \\\"wix:image: //v1/11062b_7124ff06fc56495f4846ff000.jpg/_.jpg#originWidth=1920\u0026originHeight=1080\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the image shown in the video player before the video is played.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `poster` property changes the displayed poster to\\r\\n the poster found at the new `poster` value.\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the `poster` property returns the location of the\\r\\n current poster media file.\\r\\n\\r\\n The media file is one of the following:\\r\\n\\r\\n + An image from the [Media Manager](https://support.wix.com/en/article/about-the-media-manager).\\r\\n   URL Format: `wix:image://v1//#originWidth=\u0026originHeight=`\\r\\n + An external image URL.\\r\\n   URL Format: `http(s)://site.com/image-file.jpg`\"},{\"name\":\"src\",\"slug\":\"src\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the current video's location\",\"content\":\"let videoSrc = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").src;\\n// \\\"wix:video://v1/80c05f_be1c421575e34915ad257571c4055ee4/SampleVideo_1280x720_10mb.mp4#posterUri=80c05f_be1c421575e34915ad257571c4055ee4f001.jpg\u0026posterWidth=1280\u0026posterHeight=720\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set the current video to a video uploaded to your site\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").src = \\\"wix:video://v1/80c05f_be1c421575e34915ad257571c4055ee4/SampleVideo_1280x720_10mb.mp4#posterUri=80c05f_be1c421575e34915ad257571c4055ee4f001.jpg\u0026posterWidth=1280\u0026posterHeight=720\\\";\"},{\"title\":\"Set the current video to a YouTube video\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").src = \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VyMsDTwge18\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the file location of the current video.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `src` property changes the displayed video to\\r\\n the video found at the new `src` value.\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the `src` property returns the location of the\\r\\n current video file.\\r\\n\\r\\n The video file is one of the following:\\r\\n\\r\\n + A video from the [Media Manager](https://support.wix.com/en/article/about-the-media-manager).\\r\\n   URL Format: `wix:video://v1//#posterUri=\u0026posterWidth=\u0026posterHeight=`\\r\\n + A video from a video sharing site.\\r\\n   URL Format: `https://www.site.com/video-path`\\r\\n + An external video URL.\\r\\n   URL Format: `http(s)://site.com/video-file.mp4`\"},{\"name\":\"title\",\"slug\":\"title\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a video player's title\",\"content\":\"let title = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").title // \\\"Video Title\\\"\"},{\"title\":\"Set a video player's title\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").title = \\\"Video Title\\\";\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the title displayed in a video player.\\r\\n \u003e **Notes:**\\r\\n \u003e - Setting a video title only works when a video player is presenting a\\r\\n \u003e   video uploaded to your site.\\r\\n \u003e - Getting a video title does not work when a video player is presenting a\\r\\n \u003e   video from Facebook, Twitch, or YouTube.\"},{\"name\":\"volume\",\"slug\":\"volume\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get a video player's volume\",\"content\":\"let volume = $w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").volume // 42\"},{\"title\":\"Set a video player's volume\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myVideoPlayer\\\").volume = 42;\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"number\"},\"description\":\"Sets or gets the video player volume.\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting the `volume` property sets the video player's percentage of total\\r\\n volume. Set the value to a number between `0` and `100`.\\r\\n\\r\\n Getting the `volume` property returns the video player's current\\r\\n percentage of total volume.\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** The actual volume heard by a site visitor depends on the value of the\\r\\n `volume` property and the volume settings on the visitor's device.\"},{\"name\":\"customClassList\",\"slug\":\"custom-class-list\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Gets a list of the classes of an element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").customClassList.values(); // [\\\"className1\\\", \\\"className2\\\"]\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CustomClassList\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CustomClassList.CustomClassList\"},\"description\":\"A property that represents an element's custom CSS classes.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e This property is not yet available to all users.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can use this property to manipulate the custom CSS classes of an element. For example, \\r\\nyou can add a custom class to an element or replace an existing class with a new custom class.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCustom classes are those that you create on your site, not the predefined global classes\\r\\nthat are provided for each element.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Note:** For more information, see [Styling Elements with CSS](https://www.wix.com/velo/reference/$w/styling-elements-with-css) \\r\\n\u003e and the [MDN CSS reference docs](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/CSS).\"},{\"name\":\"deleted\",\"slug\":\"deleted\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's deleted status\",\"content\":\"const isDeleted = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted;  // true\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's deleted state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").deleted ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").restore();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element was temporarily deleted from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\nUse the [`restore`](#restore) function to restore the deleted element.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `deleted` is `true`, the element is not in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `deleted` is `false` the element is in the current DOM.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Notes:**\\r\\n\u003e - An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\u003e - In Wix Studio, an element whose `deleted` status is `false` will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide**.\"},{\"name\":\"global\",\"slug\":\"global\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is displayed on all pages\",\"content\":\"let isGlobal = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").global; // false\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element appears on all pages or only on the current page.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `global` is `true`, the element appears on all pages.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `global` is `false`, the element only appears on the current page.\"},{\"name\":\"id\",\"slug\":\"id\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the ID\",\"content\":\"let myId = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").id; // \\\"myElement\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's ID.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ID is the element's unique identifier. It is used when selecting\\r\\n elements using the [`$w()`]($w.html#$w) function.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element's `id` is set in the Editor using the [Properties panel](https://support.wix.com/en/article/how-do-i-use-the-properties-panel).\"},{\"name\":\"parent\",\"slug\":\"parent\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the parent element and the parent's ID\",\"content\":\"let parentElement = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").parent;\\n\\nlet parentId = parentElement.id; // \\\"page1\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"Node\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Node.Node\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's parent element.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome elements can contain other elements. This occurs when you drag\\r\\n an element onto a container element. The container is the `parent` of\\r\\n all the elements it contains.\\r\\n\\r\\n [`Page`]($w.Page.html), [`Header`]($w.Header.html), and\\r\\n [`Footer`]($w.Footer.html) are top-level elements and have no parent.\"},{\"name\":\"rendered\",\"slug\":\"rendered\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's rendered status\",\"content\":\"let isRendered = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").rendered;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if an element is currently in the [DOM structure](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction).\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `rendered` is `true`, the element is in the current DOM structure and\\r\\n can be used.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `rendered` is `false` the element is not in the current DOM structure.\\r\\n\\r\\n An element might not be in the DOM if it is in a [slide]($w.Slide.html) or a [state]($w.State.html)\\r\\n which is not currently showing.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the element's type\",\"content\":\"let myType = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").type; // \\\"$w.Type\\\"\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the element's type.\\r\\n\\r\\nPossible values include:\\r\\n\\r\\n - `$w.TextInput`\\r\\n - `$w.TextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RichTextBox`\\r\\n - `$w.RadioButtonGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.CheckboxGroup`\\r\\n - `$w.Dropdown`\\r\\n - `$w.SelectionTags`\\r\\n - `$w.Slider`\\r\\n - `$w.DatePicker`\\r\\n - `$w.UploadButton`\\r\\n - `$w.RatingsInput`\\r\\n - `$w.AddressInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Switch`\\r\\n - `$w.SignatureInput`\\r\\n - `$w.Captcha`\"},{\"name\":\"collapsed\",\"slug\":\"collapsed\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's collapsed status\",\"content\":\"let isCollapsed = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed; // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's collapsed state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapsed ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").expand();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").collapse();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is collapsed or expanded.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `collapsed` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the collapsed element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `hidden` element, a collapsed element doesn't take up any\\r\\n space on the page. When collapsed, elements positioned within 70 pixels\\r\\n below the collapsed element and each other move up to take the\\r\\n collapsed element's place where possible. The elements that move up\\r\\n maintain their positions relative to one another.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `collapsed` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n Elements that moved up to take the collapsed element's place on the\\r\\n page are moved back down.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an expanded element (an element whose `collapsed` property is\\r\\n `false`) is still not displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `hidden`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** in the [Layers panel](https://wix.wixanswers.com/apps/widget/v1/wix/53f85d67-f8b0-41ca-9dc8-5a16390cc74f/view/en/article/9b13ee7a-06b1-4fde-80e7-8f978d9d3195#:~:text=a%20specific%20breakpoint%3F-,Yes,-.%C2%A0You%20can%20hide) in that breakpoint. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `collapsed` property is `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `collapsed` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`collapse()`](#collapse) and [`expand()`](#expand) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Collapsed on load** in the element's Properties panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `collapsed` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\"},{\"name\":\"hidden\",\"slug\":\"hidden\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get an element's hidden status\",\"content\":\"let isHidden = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden;  // false\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's hidden state\",\"content\":\"if( $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hidden ) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").show();\\n}\\nelse {\\n  $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").hide();\\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is visible or hidden.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `hidden` is `true`, the element is not displayed on the page under\\r\\n any circumstances. However, the hidden element is still in the site's DOM. Unlike a\\r\\n `collapsed` element, a hidden element continues to\\r\\n take up the same space on the page as it did when it was visible.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `hidden` is `false`, the element _may_ be displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n However, an element whose `hidden` property is `false` is still not\\r\\n displayed if:\\r\\n\\r\\n + It is `collapsed`.\\r\\n + Its parent element is hidden or collapsed.\\r\\n + It is a slide in a [Slideshow]($w.Slideshow.html) which is\\r\\n   currently not being displayed.\\r\\n + In Wix Studio, it has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n Even if the element is not displayed due to the conditions\\r\\n mentioned above, if its `hidden` property is set to `false`, it's\\r\\n displayed when the conditions no longer apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n To determine if the element is actually visible, use the\\r\\n [`isVisible`](#isVisible) property.\\r\\n\\r\\n To set the `hidden` property on an element, use the element's\\r\\n [`hide()`](#hide) or [`show()`](#show) functions.\\r\\n\\r\\n If you select **Hidden** in the Properties and Events panel\\r\\n in the Editor, the `hidden` property is set to `true` when the page loads.\\r\\n\\r\\n \u003e **Note:** An element's `hidden` property is not the same as its\\r\\n  [isVisible](#isVisible) property. The `hidden` property\\r\\n  indicates whether the element _should_ be displayed, while `isVisible`\\r\\n  indicates if it is actually displayed.\"},{\"name\":\"isVisible\",\"slug\":\"is-visible\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get whether an element is visible\",\"content\":\"let isVisible = $w(\\\"#myElement\\\").isVisible;  // true\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"boolean\"},\"description\":\"Indicates if the element is actually visible.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf `isVisible` is `true`, the element is displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n If `isVisible` is `false`, the element is not displayed on the page.\\r\\n\\r\\n The value of the `isVisible` property is calculated based on the\\r\\n `hidden`, `collapsed`, `rendered`, \\r\\n and `deleted` properties of the element and all of its ancestors. \\r\\n `isVisible` is `true` only the element is displayed on the page. \\r\\n This means that for the element and its ancestors, `rendered` is `true` and `hidden`, \\r\\n `collapsed`, and `deleted` are `false`.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e **Notes:** \\r\\n\u003e + An element's `isVisible` property is not the same as its\\r\\n\u003e   `hidden` property. The `isVisible` property\\r\\n\u003e   indicates whether the element is actually displayed, while `hidden`\\r\\n\u003e   indicates if it _should_ be displayed.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + The `isVisible` property of an element remains `true` even if\\r\\n\u003e   another element completely covers it so that a user cannot see it.\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e\\r\\n\u003e + In Wix Studio, even if the `isVisible` property of the element is `true`, it will not be displayed if the element has been set to **Hide** for the current breakpoint in the Layers more actions menu.\"}]},{\"name\":\"ViewChangeEvent\",\"slug\":\"view-change-event\",\"fqn\":\"ViewChangeEvent\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[{\"name\":\"context\",\"slug\":\"context\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the context of the event\",\"content\":\"// non-repeater event\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewChange((event) =\u003e {\\n  let type = event.context.type; // \\\"GLOBAL_SCOPE\\\"\\n});\\n\\n\\n// repeater event\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myRepeatedElement\\\").onViewChange( (event) =\u003e {\\n  let $item = $w.at(event.context)\\n  $item(\\\"#anotherRepeatedElement\\\").value = \\\"new value\\\";\\n\\n  let itemId = event.context.itemId;  // \\\"item1\\\"\\n});\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"EventContext\",\"referenceFqn\":\"Event.EventContext\"},\"description\":\"Gets the context in which an event was triggered.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn event's `context` contains information about the circumstances\\r\\n surrounding the firing of the event.\\r\\n The context property only appears in events on repeated elements.\\r\\n\\r\\n You can use the event context with [`$w.at()`]($w.html#at) to get a\\r\\n selector function which selects items from a specific repeater item.\\r\\n It contains an object with one key:value pair. The key is \\\"itemId\\\" and\\r\\n the value is the ID of the repeated item on which the event occurred.\"},{\"name\":\"options\",\"slug\":\"options\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the event options of the target element\",\"content\":\"$w.onReady(function () {\\n  $w('#myAppointmentField').onViewChange(viewChangeHandler, viewChangeOperation, 3);\\n});\\n\\nexport async function viewChangeOperation({ operationOptions }) {\\n  const { startDate, endDate } = operationOptions;\\n  let enabledDates = await myGetEnabledDatesFunction({ startDateTime: startDate, endDateTime: endDate })\\n  return slots\\n}\\n\\nexport async function viewChangeHandler(event) {\\n  const { options } = event;\\n  const slots = options.operationResult.enabledDates; \\n}\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"ViewChangeEventOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"ViewChangeEvent.ViewChangeEventOptions\"},\"description\":\"Gets the options that relate to the date picker or appointment field view change event.\"},{\"name\":\"type\",\"slug\":\"type\",\"isReadOnly\":true,\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Get the type of the event\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").onViewChange((event) =\u003e {\\n  let eventType = event.type; \\n});\"}],\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Gets the type of event that was triggered.\"}],\"articles\":[]},{\"name\":\"ViewportMixin\",\"slug\":\"viewport-mixin\",\"fqn\":\"ViewportMixin\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[],\"webhooks\":[],\"articles\":[],\"builderTypes\":[],\"properties\":[]},{\"name\":\"WixComments\",\"slug\":\"wix-comments\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments\",\"standaloneTypes\":[],\"metadata\":{},\"actions\":[{\"name\":\"closeCommentBoxes\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments.closeCommentBoxes\",\"slug\":\"close-comment-boxes\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Close all comment boxes\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").closeCommentBoxes();\"}],\"description\":\"Closes all comment boxes on the `WixComments` element.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `closeCommentBoxes()` function closes all open comment boxes.\\r\\n\\r\\nA comment box is the the input area where visitors can write comments.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere can be up to two comment boxes on the `WixComments` element. They are displayed at the top and bottom of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"lock\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments.lock\",\"slug\":\"lock\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Lock the comments widget\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").lock();\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's locked state\",\"content\":\"if ($w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").locked) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").unlock();\\n  } else {\\n    $w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").lock();\\n  }\"}],\"description\":\"Locks the `WixComments` element.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `lock()` function locks the `WixComments` element, which blocks visitors from creating or editing comments. It sets the [`locked`](#locked) property to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onCommentCountChange\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments.onCommentCountChange\",\"slug\":\"on-comment-count-change\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"callback\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Add an event handler for counting comments in the comment widget\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").onCommentCountChange( (count) =\u003e {\\n  console.log(`Comments count: ${count}`);\\n});\"},{\"title\":\"Add an event handler to display the comment count in a text element\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").onCommentCountChange((count) =\u003e {\\n  $w('#myText').text = `Total Comments: ${count}`;\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"callback\",\"slug\":\"callback\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"OnCommentCountChangeCallback\",\"referenceFqn\":\"OnCommentCountChangeCallback\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The callback function that runs when a comment is added or removed from the `WixComments` element.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when a comment is added or removed from the `WixComments` element.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `onCommentCountChange()` function adds an event handler that runs when a comment is added or removed from the `WixComments` element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onCommentCreate\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments.onCommentCreate\",\"slug\":\"on-comment-create\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"callback\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Add an event handler for when a new comment is created\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").onCommentCreate((widgetComment) =\u003e { \\n  console.log(widgetComment);\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"callback\",\"slug\":\"callback\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"OnCommentCreateCallback\",\"referenceFqn\":\"OnCommentCreateCallback\",\"isFunction\":true},\"description\":\"The callback function that is called when a new comment is created.\"}],\"description\":\"Adds an event handler that runs when a new comment is created in the `WixComments` element.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `onCommentCreate()` function sets a callback function that is called when a new comment is created in the `WixComments` element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"openNearestCommentBox\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments.openNearestCommentBox\",\"slug\":\"open-nearest-comment-box\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"}},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Open a comment box with no options\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").openNearestCommentBox();\"},{\"title\":\"Open a comment box with options\",\"content\":\"const commentBoxOptions = {\\n  focus: true,\\n  scroll: false\\n};\\n\\n$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").openNearestCommentBox(commentBoxOptions);\"},{\"title\":\"Open a comment box with an button click event\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myButton\\\").onClick( () =\u003e {\\n  $w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").openNearestCommentBox();\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"commentBoxOptions\",\"slug\":\"comment-box-options\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"REFERENCE\",\"name\":\"CommentBoxOptions\",\"referenceFqn\":\"CommentBoxOptions\"},\"description\":\"Effect options for opening the comment box.\"}],\"description\":\"Opens the comment box closest to the element that called the function.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `openNearestCommentBox()` function opens the comment box that is closest to the element that called the function.\\r\\n\\r\\nA comment box is the the input area where visitors can write a comment.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere can be up to two comment boxes on the `WixComments` element. They are displayed at the top and bottom of the element.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"setResourceId\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments.setResourceId\",\"slug\":\"set-resource-id\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"requiredProperties\":[\"resourceId\"],\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Set a comment thread resource ID\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").setResourceId(\\\"thread-2\\\");\"},{\"title\":\"Navigate between comment threads using button clicks\",\"content\":\"// Set the resourceId to an image on the page.\\n$w(\\\"#myButton2\\\").onClick(() =\u003e {\\n  $w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").setResourceId(\\\"sunsetImage\\\");\\n});\"}],\"actionParams\":[{\"name\":\"resourceId\",\"slug\":\"resource-id\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"type\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"The unique resource ID for the new comment thread.\"}],\"description\":\"Retrieves a comment thread with a unique resource ID, or creates one if it doesn't exist.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `setResourceId()` function replaces the comments thread in the `WixComments` element with a different comment thread. You can create new comment threads and transition between threads by calling the function. \\r\\n\\r\\nEach comment thread is referenced by a unique resource ID that is arbitrarily chosen when the function is first called on that thread.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"unlock\",\"fqn\":\"WixComments.unlock\",\"slug\":\"unlock\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Unlock the comments widget\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"myCommentsWidget\\\").unlock();\"},{\"title\":\"Toggle an element's locked state\",\"content\":\"if ($w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").locked) {\\n  $w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").unlock();\\n  } else {\\n    $w(\\\"#myCommentsWidget\\\").lock();\\n  }\"}],\"description\":\"Unlocks the `WixComments` element.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `unlock()` function unlocks the `WixComments` element, restoring comment functionality. It sets the [`locked`](#locked) property to `false`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"delete\",\"fqn\":\"Element.delete\",\"slug\":\"delete\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"isInternal\":false,\"actionErrors\":[],\"isDeveloperPreview\":false,\"maturity\":\"GA\",\"adminMethod\":false,\"returnType\":{\"kind\":\"PROMISE\",\"argumentType\":{\"kind\":\"PRIMITIVE\",\"name\":\"void\"},\"description\":\"Fulfilled - When the element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\"},\"examples\":[{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete();\"},{\"title\":\"Delete an element from the DOM and log a message when done\",\"content\":\"$w(\\\"#myElement\\\").delete()\\n  .then( () =\u003e {\\n    console.log(\\\"Done with delete\\\");\\n  } );\"}],\"description\":\"Deletes an element from the [DOM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document_Object_Model/Introduction). \\r\\nThis is a temporary deletion. Use [`restore`](#restore) to restore the deleted element.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSEO crawlers cannot find content in an element whose `deleted` status is `true`. \\r\\nContent in an element that is in `hidden` status can be found by crawlers.\\r\\n\\r\\n\u003e**Note:** An element whose `deleted` status is `true` can be edited.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `delete()` function returns a Promise that is resolved when the\\r\\n element's `deleted` property has been set to `true`.\",\"sdkErrors\":[]},{\"name\":\"onMouseIn\",\"fqn\":\"Element.onMouseIn\",\"slug\":\"on-mouse-in\",\"isDeprecated\":false,\"